00:16:34.809 --> 00:16:38.280
There's an exercise that I often
do with my first-year students.


00:16:38.313 --> 00:16:40.749
I have them research mainstream
economic publications


00:16:40.781 --> 00:16:43.451
from the 16th
to the 21st century,


00:16:43.484 --> 00:16:46.754
trying to find any mention of
basic sustainability principles.


00:16:46.788 --> 00:16:49.124
And each year the students
come back stunned


00:16:49.156 --> 00:16:51.192
by how this period
gave no priority


00:16:51.226 --> 00:16:53.662
to even the most obvious
regenerative science.


00:16:53.694 --> 00:16:56.631
Let alone anything
related to public health.


00:16:56.664 --> 00:16:58.867
Such things were
considered external


00:16:58.900 --> 00:17:00.602
to this contrived,
competitive game


00:17:00.635 --> 00:17:02.636
they called business.


00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:05.740
Here you had
an entire global civilization


00:17:05.772 --> 00:17:08.876
powering itself through
the mechanism of consuming.


00:17:08.909 --> 00:17:11.612
That's literally what drove
their economy as absurd


00:17:11.646 --> 00:17:14.249
as that sounds.
And the more people bought


00:17:14.281 --> 00:17:16.417
and consumed,
the more demand for jobs.


00:17:16.451 --> 00:17:18.886
Hence more circulating
purchasing power


00:17:18.919 --> 00:17:21.489
to again be spent on consuming.


00:17:21.522 --> 00:17:24.192
Endlessly and viciously
repeating.


00:17:24.224 --> 00:17:26.427
That was the economic
system back then.


00:17:26.461 --> 00:17:28.663
And to think any part
of that would be workable


00:17:28.695 --> 00:17:33.201
in the long run, on a finite
planet, is pure lunacy.


00:17:33.233 --> 00:17:35.203
To make matters worse,
the system was rooted


00:17:35.235 --> 00:17:38.639
in strategic human exploitation,
which structurally ensured


00:17:38.673 --> 00:17:41.510
large wealth and power
differences between groups,


00:17:41.542 --> 00:17:45.446
and the long term cultural result
was very poor social integrity.


00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:49.451
Racism, xenophobia, sexism
and other forms of bigotry


00:17:49.483 --> 00:17:52.587
were an inevitable side effect
of this kind of social system


00:17:52.619 --> 00:17:55.256
ultimately rooted
in class stratification,


00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:58.593
otherwise known
as socio-economic inequality.


00:17:58.626 --> 00:18:00.295
And when you put
it all together,


00:18:00.328 --> 00:18:02.396
you realize a deep
social pathology.


00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:05.667
A pathology that not only
severely limited human potential,


00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:09.237
actually bringing out the worst of
our biological and social nature,


00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:12.473
but one that was blindly pushing
civilization toward oblivion,


00:18:12.507 --> 00:18:14.476
due to accelerating
ecological decline


00:18:14.509 --> 00:18:16.678
and systemic human conflict.


00:18:17.678 --> 00:18:19.613
By the time we
reached the 21st century


00:18:19.646 --> 00:18:22.317
the consequences
of all this weren't subtle.


00:18:22.349 --> 00:18:25.386
We're talking massive global
inequity and poverty,


00:18:25.419 --> 00:18:28.622
relentless worldwide conflict,
endless power abuses


00:18:28.655 --> 00:18:30.325
and systematic oppression,


00:18:30.357 --> 00:18:32.560
not to mention
the near irreversible


00:18:32.594 --> 00:18:35.197
decline of all life
support systems.


00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:37.531
And while it seems
obvious to us today,


00:18:37.565 --> 00:18:39.868
you have to understand
the kind of indoctrination


00:18:39.901 --> 00:18:41.403
that occurred back then.


00:18:41.435 --> 00:18:42.937
The culture was so conditioned


00:18:42.971 --> 00:18:44.638
by the dominant worldview,


00:18:44.672 --> 00:18:46.942
they just couldn't recognize
the flaws inherent


00:18:46.974 --> 00:18:49.477
to the structure
of their society.


00:18:50.377 --> 00:18:53.915
So by force of this,
they engaged in very superficial activism


00:18:53.947 --> 00:18:56.984
centered around political
institutions that really were


00:18:57.018 --> 00:18:58.953
just a parody of themselves.


00:19:00.288 --> 00:19:01.723
Attempts at social change


00:19:01.755 --> 00:19:03.557
were deeply fragmented in focus


00:19:03.590 --> 00:19:05.260
because people's understanding


00:19:05.292 --> 00:19:06.962
of cause and effect
was so shallow.


00:19:06.994 --> 00:19:08.963
So the whole thing
just became a spectacle.


00:19:08.996 --> 00:19:11.498
And endless blame game
between groups.


00:19:11.531 --> 00:19:13.534
Their so-called
democratic process


00:19:13.568 --> 00:19:16.637
centered not on actual policy,
but around these political


00:19:16.671 --> 00:19:20.242
institutions that seemed to
vaguely represent such policy.


00:19:20.274 --> 00:19:23.944
A true democracy as we now know
allows for public consensus


00:19:23.978 --> 00:19:25.947
on actual issues
not the appointment


00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:28.650
of representatives to make
those decisions for them.


00:19:28.683 --> 00:19:30.751
That's not
really democracy at all.


00:19:30.784 --> 00:19:33.921
That's simply a watered-down
version of authoritarianism,


00:19:33.954 --> 00:19:35.691
voting for kings and queens.


00:19:36.624 --> 00:19:38.425
And to add insult to injury,


00:19:38.459 --> 00:19:40.828
because society was rooted
in this business system


00:19:40.861 --> 00:19:44.365
of property and trade
everything was for sale.


00:19:44.398 --> 00:19:47.434
People loved to argue
about moral lines and ethics,


00:19:47.467 --> 00:19:50.471
but the fact was politicians,
and hence policy,


00:19:50.504 --> 00:19:53.474
was just another commodity
to be bought and sold.


00:19:53.508 --> 00:19:56.877
So inevitably those who did
end up with true social power


00:19:56.911 --> 00:19:58.813
were the ones
with the most wealth.


00:19:58.846 --> 00:20:00.749
That wasn't a corruption,


00:20:00.781 --> 00:20:03.018
that was simply
the nature of the system.


00:20:04.049 --> 00:20:06.521
And needless to say this
business power subculture


00:20:06.553 --> 00:20:09.623
was certainly the least likely
to want to change the very system


00:20:09.656 --> 00:20:12.293
that had so disproportionately
rewarded them.


00:20:13.528 --> 00:20:16.564
And as science and technology
increased efficiency


00:20:16.597 --> 00:20:19.867
creating higher material
standards of living in general


00:20:19.901 --> 00:20:23.471
the lack of human rights
progress and the anti-democratic


00:20:23.503 --> 00:20:27.074
nature of society
became increasingly masked.


00:20:27.107 --> 00:20:29.944
People's dignity
and integrity were bought off


00:20:29.976 --> 00:20:32.880
by gadgets and toys
and addictions.


00:20:32.914 --> 00:20:35.450
Feeding a materialist fetish


00:20:35.482 --> 00:20:37.618
that so distracted
the minds of many.


00:20:38.653 --> 00:20:40.689
<i>And you know,
I often ponder all this,</i>


00:20:40.722 --> 00:20:42.089
<i>trying to put myself
in the shoes</i>


00:20:42.123 --> 00:20:44.025
<i>of the average person back then,</i>


00:20:44.058 --> 00:20:47.028
<i>especially in the more affluent
and highly unequal regions,</i>


00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:49.630
<i>such as
the United States of America,</i>


00:20:49.664 --> 00:20:51.633
<i>and it really makes me shudder.</i>


00:20:51.665 --> 00:20:54.903
<i>People stuck in traffic,
piling into these office prisons</i>


00:20:54.935 --> 00:20:58.740
<i>to push paper around,
engaging meaningless occupations</i>


00:20:58.772 --> 00:21:01.675
<i>that wasted far more energy
and wealth than they created</i>


00:21:01.709 --> 00:21:04.546
<i>so they can continue buying
these things they don't need,</i>


00:21:04.578 --> 00:21:07.514
<i>elevating their artificial
status and so on.</i>


00:21:07.548 --> 00:21:09.550
<i>It's like a bad horror movie.</i>


00:25:07.120 --> 00:25:09.723
If there's any historical
through-line that reveals


00:25:09.757 --> 00:25:12.626
how important a system-based
worldview is,


00:25:12.659 --> 00:25:15.963
both in understanding society
and knowing how to change it,


00:25:15.996 --> 00:25:18.999
it's a long history of slavery
and human exploitation.


00:25:19.032 --> 00:25:22.203
You can't have a society that's
based upon hierarchical power


00:25:22.235 --> 00:25:24.705
and specialized labor,
where people are seen


00:25:24.739 --> 00:25:26.841
as economic tools to be used


00:25:26.874 --> 00:25:29.210
strategically
for another's differential gain,


00:25:29.242 --> 00:25:32.746
and ever expect
high moral integrity.


00:25:32.780 --> 00:25:35.849
Consider the
function of cost efficiency.


00:25:35.883 --> 00:25:39.053
Cost efficiency is about trying
to save money on production


00:25:39.086 --> 00:25:42.056
in order to maximize profit
upon final sale.


00:25:42.088 --> 00:25:44.626
It's at the core
of the basic gaming strategy


00:25:44.658 --> 00:25:46.793
that's required
in market economics.


00:25:46.827 --> 00:25:50.397
And that simple incentive, the
principle of seeking to reduce


00:25:50.431 --> 00:25:54.402
input costs to maximize
output gains is at the root


00:25:54.434 --> 00:25:58.705
of thousands of years of human
slavery in one form or another.


00:25:58.739 --> 00:26:01.876
Whether indentured servitude,
bonded labor,


00:26:01.908 --> 00:26:05.146
chattel slavery in earlier
times to human trafficking


00:26:05.178 --> 00:26:08.215
and debt driven wage slavery
in more modern times.


00:26:09.149 --> 00:26:12.052
And the point to make here
is that this kind of framework


00:26:12.086 --> 00:26:15.189
was so normalized
by the turn of the 21st century,


00:26:15.222 --> 00:26:18.792
a period, by the way, that had
more slaves in absolute numbers


00:26:18.826 --> 00:26:20.662
than any time in human history.


00:26:20.694 --> 00:26:23.330
The average person still
didn't see the connection.


00:26:23.364 --> 00:26:27.135
They had been conditioned by
these mythical free market ideas


00:26:27.167 --> 00:26:29.670
arguing that because
people could now choose


00:26:29.703 --> 00:26:32.139
which area of the economy
to submit their labor to,


00:26:32.173 --> 00:26:35.777
choose which company to be
subordinated, or perhaps get the capital


00:26:35.809 --> 00:26:38.745
and start their own company
and then choose who to exploit


00:26:38.779 --> 00:26:40.381
for their own personal
advantage.


00:26:40.414 --> 00:26:43.017
Somehow coercion
just no longer existed.


00:26:43.050 --> 00:26:44.819
That was the illusion.


00:26:44.851 --> 00:26:48.321
And any advanced technological
society that evolves


00:26:48.355 --> 00:26:52.326
not to organize an effort
to provide basic life support


00:26:52.358 --> 00:26:55.228
to its citizens allowing them
to pursue their own interest


00:26:55.261 --> 00:26:58.832
on their own terms,
instead structurally forcing


00:26:58.866 --> 00:27:02.436
everyone to fight with
each other for basic survival,


00:27:02.470 --> 00:27:04.838
for not defendable
reason mind you,


00:27:04.871 --> 00:27:07.240
is not a free society at all.


00:27:07.273 --> 00:27:09.710
It's a system
of violence and oppression


00:27:09.743 --> 00:27:13.348
regardless of how materially
wealthy that society may appear.


00:27:14.248 --> 00:27:17.419
Now, all that said,
it's important to consider...


00:29:27.181 --> 00:29:29.450
You have meddled
with the primal forces


00:29:29.482 --> 00:29:31.251
of nature, Mr. Beale.


00:29:34.221 --> 00:29:38.126
And you will atone.


00:29:41.595 --> 00:29:43.064
It's been a long time, Simon.


00:29:43.097 --> 00:29:44.598
So, the reason
you're here with me


00:29:44.632 --> 00:29:47.435
and not in some vassal
state being tortured


00:29:47.467 --> 00:29:50.337
is because the GSA
needs your help.


00:29:50.370 --> 00:29:53.340
We're being overrun by a group
of hackers and they appear to be


00:29:53.374 --> 00:29:56.277
advancing their abilities
faster than we can counter.


00:29:56.309 --> 00:29:57.412
Orion.


00:29:59.012 --> 00:30:01.014
That's right. Orion.


00:30:01.048 --> 00:30:02.884
We have been tracking them
for years.


00:30:02.916 --> 00:30:04.184
Luddite anarchists.


00:30:04.217 --> 00:30:05.452
They want to return civilization


00:30:05.485 --> 00:30:07.354
to the Stone Age.


00:30:07.387 --> 00:30:09.624
We figure if they continue
their rate of progress,


00:30:09.656 --> 00:30:12.460
we only have a few weeks
before they breach.


00:30:12.492 --> 00:30:15.128
- Taking control of our systems.
- That'd be bad.


00:30:15.162 --> 00:30:18.266
Hence our priorities.
As aggravating as your little


00:30:18.299 --> 00:30:22.237
Concordia project has been,
you were never this distasteful.


00:30:23.303 --> 00:30:26.206
You do realize
that even if Orion is stopped,


00:30:26.240 --> 00:30:28.209
another insurgency,
likely more malicious,


00:30:28.242 --> 00:30:29.911
is just around the corner,
right?


00:30:31.444 --> 00:30:33.179
- Your point?
- My point


00:30:33.213 --> 00:30:35.383
is one way to measure
the integrity of a society


00:30:35.415 --> 00:30:37.451
is by how many outliers
it creates.


00:30:37.483 --> 00:30:40.521
Violent criminals, inner-city
gangs, serial killers,


00:30:40.553 --> 00:30:42.355
mass murderers, terrorists,


00:30:42.388 --> 00:30:45.959
to now this lovely hacker
dystopia you've inspired.


00:30:45.992 --> 00:30:47.928
You have a systemic problem,
Simon,


00:30:47.962 --> 00:30:49.430
and it's only going to grow.


00:30:50.630 --> 00:30:52.666
You're looking
through the wrong lens, John.


00:30:52.700 --> 00:30:54.936
And unlike the past,
the outliers now


00:30:54.969 --> 00:30:56.971
have exponentially
advancing technology.


00:30:57.003 --> 00:31:00.340
Some disgruntled kid fashioning
a Molotov cocktail years ago,


00:31:00.374 --> 00:31:03.511
can now create weapons of mass
destruction, or in this case weapons


00:31:03.543 --> 00:31:05.612
of mass disturbance
with little more effort.


00:31:06.680 --> 00:31:10.418
Again, you're looking
through the wrong lens.


00:31:10.451 --> 00:31:13.087
No one ever said
the natural course of humanity


00:31:13.119 --> 00:31:14.454
was going to be pretty.


00:31:14.488 --> 00:31:16.090
So it's natural
for humanity to flirt


00:31:16.123 --> 00:31:19.093
with its own destruction?
And increasingly so?


00:31:19.126 --> 00:31:20.929
Because that's
where all this leads.


00:31:21.761 --> 00:31:25.465
Since the dawn of civilization,
those with the most advanced


00:31:25.499 --> 00:31:28.269
tools are the ones
who set the stage.


00:31:28.301 --> 00:31:31.638
From the rock, to the sword,
to the gun, to the bomb,


00:31:31.672 --> 00:31:35.343
to AI,
a sociological law of nature


00:31:35.376 --> 00:31:38.445
rooted in our evolutionary
psychology.


00:31:38.479 --> 00:31:41.682
And if this race happens
to lead to destruction,


00:31:41.714 --> 00:31:45.419
well,
such is the natural course.


00:31:46.453 --> 00:31:49.557
Only human conceit
assumes otherwise.


00:31:54.060 --> 00:31:56.230
I see you haven't lost
that charming nihilism.


00:31:57.196 --> 00:31:58.632
- Drink?
- No.


00:32:00.334 --> 00:32:04.105
And it's not nihilism, John,
it's realism.


00:32:05.239 --> 00:32:08.242
Conflict is what makes
the world go round.


00:32:09.475 --> 00:32:12.981
And whomever wins
defines the course.


00:32:23.257 --> 00:32:24.692
- So what's the deal?
- The deal is


00:32:24.724 --> 00:32:27.293
you help us tame the barbarians
at the gate


00:32:27.327 --> 00:32:30.297
along with anything else we ask.


00:32:30.329 --> 00:32:32.133
In return,


00:32:32.165 --> 00:32:35.101
you'll be granted
a decent life here.


00:32:35.135 --> 00:32:36.771
This ship might be
a place of work,


00:32:36.803 --> 00:32:39.607
but it's also
a self-contained city.


00:32:40.674 --> 00:32:45.078
We go back a long way, John,
and despite our differences,


00:32:45.111 --> 00:32:47.747
I would hate to see
that genius go to waste.


00:32:47.780 --> 00:32:48.782
And if I don't?


00:32:50.283 --> 00:32:52.619
You know the answer to that.


00:32:52.653 --> 00:32:55.756
Aside from this possible
Orion catastrophe,


00:32:55.789 --> 00:32:58.526
which I doubt
your humanist ego would allow,


00:32:59.693 --> 00:33:02.530
you'll be turned over
to interrogation


00:33:02.562 --> 00:33:05.232
and it won't be cinematic.


00:33:06.332 --> 00:33:10.070
Either way,
you're not leaving this ship.


00:33:12.572 --> 00:33:15.475
Okay, Simon,
but I have one condition.


00:33:16.542 --> 00:33:19.079
I want you to put an end
to program UX83.


00:33:20.547 --> 00:33:22.650
Otherwise known
as the Malthusian Mandate.


00:33:28.355 --> 00:33:30.491
If you knew about the Mandate,


00:33:30.523 --> 00:33:32.525
why hasn't Concordia leaked it?


00:33:32.559 --> 00:33:34.528
Never had a complete picture.


00:33:34.560 --> 00:33:37.598
- And what do you think you're missing?
- Good question.


00:33:37.630 --> 00:33:39.632
We find a cryptically
mentioned in documents


00:33:39.665 --> 00:33:41.769
related to the GSA's
control programs.


00:33:42.668 --> 00:33:44.571
It appears the Mandate
was employed in the death


00:33:44.605 --> 00:33:47.374
of at least 20 million
last year alone.


00:33:47.406 --> 00:33:49.676
How this is occurring
and why is not clear.


00:33:50.810 --> 00:33:52.346
So why don't you enlighten me?


00:36:19.526 --> 00:36:22.796
So you wrote a book
called <i>The Neolithic Maladaptation</i>


00:36:22.828 --> 00:36:25.265
which focuses
on the nature of culture


00:36:25.298 --> 00:36:27.967
before the Great Transition.


00:36:28.001 --> 00:36:31.671
Can you clarify
what you meant by this title?


00:36:31.705 --> 00:36:35.776
Sure. So I think the defining
question of civilization


00:36:35.809 --> 00:36:39.479
is what characteristics
enable us to survive and prosper


00:36:39.513 --> 00:36:42.383
sustainably and peacefully
over generational time.


00:36:43.450 --> 00:36:46.419
Thousands of years ago,
upon the advent of agriculture,


00:36:46.452 --> 00:36:49.389
the Neolithic Revolution,
we found ourselves


00:36:49.423 --> 00:36:52.325
in a new social arrangement,
a new structure,


00:36:52.359 --> 00:36:55.529
one that would later prove
to be highly incompatible.


00:36:55.562 --> 00:36:57.731
Not only incompatible
with the habitat,


00:36:57.763 --> 00:36:59.767
inherently unsustainable
since the economy


00:36:59.800 --> 00:37:02.303
literally required
consumption and growth,


00:37:02.336 --> 00:37:05.571
but also incompatible
with our very social nature.


00:37:05.604 --> 00:37:09.776
And, long story short, humans
are simply not meant to exist


00:37:09.810 --> 00:37:12.346
in an economically
stratified society


00:37:12.379 --> 00:37:15.582
if the expectation is high
levels of public health


00:37:15.615 --> 00:37:17.417
and peaceful coexistence.


00:37:17.450 --> 00:37:19.586
It's always interesting
to review the work


00:37:19.618 --> 00:37:22.655
of mainstream scientists
at the turn of the 21st century


00:37:22.689 --> 00:37:24.992
as they desperately try
to convince themselves


00:37:25.024 --> 00:37:26.926
that a competitive,
exploitative,


00:37:26.959 --> 00:37:30.463
vainly status seeking mindset
was an inalterable expression


00:37:30.497 --> 00:37:33.500
of human nature,
when the fact is our genes,


00:37:33.533 --> 00:37:36.002
our biology and how
the environment interacts


00:37:36.035 --> 00:37:40.540
with our evolved selves allows
for a vast range of orientations


00:37:40.573 --> 00:37:44.644
with narrow self-interest,
greed, merely part of that range.


00:37:44.678 --> 00:37:47.948
If we've proven to be anything,
it's adaptable.


00:37:47.981 --> 00:37:49.917
There's certainly
no blank slate.


00:37:49.950 --> 00:37:52.618
We're not infinitely malleable,


00:37:52.651 --> 00:37:55.054
but it has been grossly
underestimated historically


00:37:55.088 --> 00:37:57.591
just how wide
our range of adaptive


00:37:57.624 --> 00:38:00.694
potential really is.
And what most determines


00:38:00.727 --> 00:38:04.131
which behavioral traits
will define a society's culture


00:38:04.164 --> 00:38:06.100
is its social structure.


00:38:06.133 --> 00:38:10.136
Or more specifically,
that structure's economic basis.


00:38:10.169 --> 00:38:13.072
The method
by which we must survive.


00:38:13.106 --> 00:38:15.975
<i>If that structure
rewards competition, dominance,</i>


00:38:16.008 --> 00:38:18.444
<i>and narrow self-interest,
then the culture</i>


00:38:18.477 --> 00:38:21.013
<i>will predominantly
express those values.</i>


00:38:21.046 --> 00:38:25.385
<i>If it rewards collaboration,
empathy and pro-social concern,</i>


00:38:25.419 --> 00:38:29.690
<i>the resulting culture will
predominantly express those values.</i>


00:38:29.722 --> 00:38:31.624
For the majority
of human history,


00:38:31.658 --> 00:38:33.827
before the advent
of agriculture,


00:38:33.859 --> 00:38:35.662
We lived in non-hierarchical,


00:38:35.694 --> 00:38:37.798
non-competitive
social arrangements.


00:38:37.830 --> 00:38:40.700
Why? Because the economic
basis of survival


00:38:40.734 --> 00:38:42.636
actually incentivized


00:38:42.669 --> 00:38:45.373
sharing and collaboration,
and not the opposite.


00:38:46.472 --> 00:38:49.575
So what I mean by maladaptation
is while humanity


00:38:49.609 --> 00:38:52.045
did successfully adapt
to the survival requisites


00:38:52.077 --> 00:38:53.880
born from
the Neolithic Revolution,


00:38:53.914 --> 00:38:55.649
the resulting social structure,


00:38:55.682 --> 00:38:58.819
the system that became codified,
proved maladapted.


00:38:58.852 --> 00:39:01.655
<i>The economic system
was simply incompatible</i>


00:39:01.687 --> 00:39:05.758
<i>with what was required for humanity
to be sustainable in the long-term.</i>


00:39:05.792 --> 00:39:08.796
<i>Failing our need to integrate
properly with the ecosystem</i>


00:39:08.828 --> 00:39:12.999
<i>while limiting our ability to
coexist peacefully with each other.</i>


00:39:13.033 --> 00:39:15.669
And by the time of
the Industrial Revolution


00:39:15.702 --> 00:39:18.037
in the 19th century,
these flaws were rapidly


00:39:18.071 --> 00:39:19.873
coming to the surface.


00:39:19.906 --> 00:39:22.476
Conditions had changed and
if it wasn't for our dramatic


00:39:22.508 --> 00:39:24.744
transformation to break out
of that system,


00:39:24.778 --> 00:39:27.714
there is little question,
society would have seen total


00:39:27.747 --> 00:39:31.018
ecologically collapse combined
with catastrophic global war.


00:39:33.153 --> 00:39:35.656
So it must be
difficult to look back


00:39:35.689 --> 00:39:37.790
at that time given
what we know now.


00:39:37.823 --> 00:39:40.493
It seems like things should have
changed much sooner, right?


00:39:40.526 --> 00:39:43.563
Sure, but it reveals
that as much as we'd like


00:39:43.597 --> 00:39:46.098
to believe we're rational,
objective beings,


00:39:46.131 --> 00:39:49.970
we're actually bound
by deep social vulnerability.


00:39:50.002 --> 00:39:53.540
We are social beings first
and intellectual beings second.


00:39:54.240 --> 00:39:57.210
What you see back then
is a kind of mass hypnosis


00:39:57.243 --> 00:39:59.078
that paralyzed society,


00:39:59.111 --> 00:40:01.581
keeping people short-sighted
and fearful,


00:40:01.615 --> 00:40:04.051
prone to conform to the values
and practices of those


00:40:04.084 --> 00:40:07.553
who happen to be winning
in the contrived economic game.


00:40:07.586 --> 00:40:10.723
One glance at the media from
back then gives it all away.


00:40:10.756 --> 00:40:13.260
Status posturing,
people obsessed with appearing


00:40:13.292 --> 00:40:17.164
affluent, accomplished, loved,
famous, beautiful.


00:40:17.196 --> 00:40:20.767
All a kind of pathological
emulation of those of high


00:40:20.800 --> 00:40:25.138
socioeconomic status,
billionaires, celebrities.


00:40:25.171 --> 00:40:27.675
As one notable philosopher
stated long ago,


00:40:34.247 --> 00:40:36.984
So once again
it all begs the question,


00:40:37.017 --> 00:40:40.053
what actually defines success
in the human condition?


00:40:40.086 --> 00:40:43.223
What kind of culture is most
optimized to sustain itself


00:40:43.256 --> 00:40:46.593
over time while, of course,
being happy and stable?


00:40:46.626 --> 00:40:48.194
And while there's
plenty to learn,


00:40:48.227 --> 00:40:50.630
we do know
what doesn't define it:


00:40:50.664 --> 00:40:54.001
the excessive materialistic
wealth and status driven neurosis


00:40:54.033 --> 00:40:57.236
so characteristic back then
has literally zero


00:40:57.269 --> 00:40:59.705
positive relationship
to long-term species


00:40:59.738 --> 00:41:02.943
sustainability and optimized
public health.


00:41:02.975 --> 00:41:05.845
In short,
the values were dead wrong.


00:41:05.879 --> 00:41:08.982
And not to sound mean, but
if I were to resort to derisive


00:41:09.015 --> 00:41:11.752
status labeling,
common to that period of time,


00:41:11.785 --> 00:41:14.721
there's no question
that the greatest failures


00:41:14.754 --> 00:41:18.025
were the ones who own mansions,
drove over priced cars,


00:41:18.057 --> 00:41:21.794
wore luxury jewelry,
maintained extremely lucrative


00:41:21.827 --> 00:41:24.063
yet completely
meaningless occupations


00:41:24.097 --> 00:41:26.232
while hoarding great wealth.


00:41:26.265 --> 00:41:28.001
What kind of sad,
insecure creature


00:41:28.033 --> 00:41:29.903
needs to flaunt such excess


00:41:29.935 --> 00:41:33.640
clearly signaling opposition
to other people's well-being?


00:41:33.673 --> 00:41:37.310
True success is reinforcing
harmony, balance.


00:41:37.343 --> 00:41:40.046
The goal is not necessarily
to become something,


00:41:40.080 --> 00:41:43.150
but to find out who
and what you truly are.


00:41:43.182 --> 00:41:45.184
And how you fit
inside the ecosystem


00:41:45.218 --> 00:41:47.287
of nature
that gave birth to you.


00:41:47.319 --> 00:41:50.356
The most successful people,
the true winners,


00:41:50.390 --> 00:41:54.995
are never the ones striving for
celebrity and material excess,


00:41:55.028 --> 00:41:58.865
they are the humble minimalists
valuing how they can contribute


00:41:58.897 --> 00:42:01.934
to the well-being
and health of everything,


00:42:01.968 --> 00:42:04.905
realizing the world
is one system,


00:42:04.937 --> 00:42:07.374
and the more they optimize
that contribution,


00:42:07.406 --> 00:42:11.111
the more truly successful
they actually become.


00:42:13.680 --> 00:42:15.982
When I look back on all this,


00:42:16.015 --> 00:42:18.082
I think what I find most tragic


00:42:18.084 --> 00:42:20.953
is the spiritual loss
of the individual.


00:42:20.986 --> 00:42:25.124
How people were fundamentally
alienated from themselves


00:42:25.158 --> 00:42:29.162
their identities hijacked
by competitive insecurity,


00:42:29.194 --> 00:42:32.198
trying to conform
to some acceptable profile


00:42:32.231 --> 00:42:34.734
that would serve
their advantage best,


00:42:34.767 --> 00:42:36.302
not who they actually are,


00:42:36.336 --> 00:42:38.939
but what the system
requires them to become.


00:44:07.359 --> 00:44:10.497
The
soul selects her own society.


00:44:10.530 --> 00:44:13.934
Then shuts the door
to her divine majority.


00:44:13.966 --> 00:44:17.269
Present no more. Unmoved.


00:44:17.303 --> 00:44:21.040
She notes the chariots
pausing at her low gate.


00:44:21.073 --> 00:44:24.343
Unmoved. An emperor
be kneeling upon her mat.


00:44:24.377 --> 00:44:29.316
I've known her from
an ample nation. Choose one.


00:44:29.348 --> 00:44:33.352
Then close the valves
of her attention. Like stone.


00:46:53.191 --> 00:46:54.560
Let me ask you, John.


00:46:55.495 --> 00:46:57.197
What do you think
the greatest form


00:46:57.229 --> 00:47:01.333
of social control is? Law? Debt?


00:47:01.367 --> 00:47:03.535
Religion.


00:47:03.568 --> 00:47:06.538
And this has what to do
with the Malthusian Mandate?


00:47:06.571 --> 00:47:09.943
- Humor me.
- I don't know.


00:47:09.975 --> 00:47:13.178
How about socialization?
People policing each other.


00:47:13.211 --> 00:47:16.949
A properly tuned culture
does regulate itself, yes.


00:47:16.982 --> 00:47:18.551
We've had the same training,
Simon.


00:47:18.584 --> 00:47:20.654
I'm just as aware of what
shapes psychology as you are.


00:47:20.687 --> 00:47:23.490
Yeah, see, I'm not so sure.


00:47:23.522 --> 00:47:25.392
I don't think we'd be
in this situation


00:47:25.425 --> 00:47:27.327
- if that was really the case.
- You mean because I actually


00:47:27.359 --> 00:47:28.461
believe the world can change?


00:47:33.098 --> 00:47:35.702
A child's born
biologically programmed


00:47:35.734 --> 00:47:38.070
to adapt to its environment.


00:47:38.104 --> 00:47:40.372
It grows,
inching through formative years,


00:47:40.406 --> 00:47:43.310
shaped by the traditions
and beliefs of culture.


00:47:43.343 --> 00:47:46.078
Institutional education
introduces structure


00:47:46.111 --> 00:47:50.149
creating comfort with authority,
regimentation, status.


00:47:50.182 --> 00:47:53.552
- Nurturing social schema.
- And a fundamental insecurity


00:47:53.586 --> 00:47:56.323
forged
by a deeply unequal world,


00:47:56.356 --> 00:47:58.191
a world of sanctioned
indifference,


00:47:58.223 --> 00:47:59.492
where compassion is weakness


00:47:59.524 --> 00:48:01.560
and domination is virtuous.


00:48:01.593 --> 00:48:04.030
What survival requires.


00:48:04.763 --> 00:48:07.200
In the current arrangement,
sure.


00:48:07.232 --> 00:48:09.970
And this early sense of
insecurity has a unique effect.


00:48:10.002 --> 00:48:13.305
Once childish tendencies we humans
are supposed to grow out of:


00:48:13.339 --> 00:48:16.977
attention-seeking, spoiled
self-interest, manipulativeness,


00:48:17.010 --> 00:48:20.046
bullying,
competition become ingrained.


00:48:20.078 --> 00:48:21.747
Maturity stunted.


00:48:21.781 --> 00:48:23.717
Setting the stage
for yet another disciple


00:48:23.749 --> 00:48:26.151
in the cult of narcissistic
individualism.


00:48:26.185 --> 00:48:28.655
Poetic.


00:48:29.789 --> 00:48:31.658
By the time higher
education is reached,


00:48:31.691 --> 00:48:35.028
formalized academia,
the stronghold of the status quo,


00:48:35.060 --> 00:48:36.997
what natural curiosity
may remain


00:48:37.030 --> 00:48:39.598
is now further constrained
by socialization.


00:48:39.631 --> 00:48:43.470
Myopic focus, detached
from the pursuit of knowledge,


00:48:43.502 --> 00:48:46.606
existing only for the sake
of commercial utility.


00:48:46.638 --> 00:48:50.676
- To define their product.
- And ultimately their identity.


00:48:50.709 --> 00:48:53.146
Becoming little more than
yet another agent of trade.


00:48:53.178 --> 00:48:56.383
A civilization reduced to
the goal of endless striving.


00:48:56.415 --> 00:48:58.417
To sell something
to someone else.


00:49:00.752 --> 00:49:03.622
The world is a business,
Mr. Beale.


00:49:05.258 --> 00:49:06.359
<i>So the cog turns.</i>


00:49:07.727 --> 00:49:10.597
<i>While in those fleeting moments
economic stress does subside,</i>


00:49:10.629 --> 00:49:12.499
<i>when the shackles do come off,</i>


00:49:12.531 --> 00:49:14.667
<i>existential turbulence blooms,</i>


00:49:14.700 --> 00:49:17.169
<i>as they desperately search
for some kind of deeper meaning</i>


00:49:17.202 --> 00:49:20.072
<i>in the daily grind.
And this emotional void,</i>


00:49:20.106 --> 00:49:23.276
<i>this state of loss, leads
the pathological escapism.</i>


00:49:23.309 --> 00:49:25.611
<i>Distraction and self-medication
become the hobby.</i>


00:49:26.646 --> 00:49:28.781
<i>So they turn to their screens</i>


00:49:28.814 --> 00:49:32.251
<i>windows of projected normality
equating freedom</i>


00:49:32.285 --> 00:49:34.453
<i>with the unattainable delusions</i>


00:49:34.486 --> 00:49:36.488
<i>of wealth, fame, honor.</i>


00:49:36.522 --> 00:49:38.290
<i>While constantly
being reminded that they are</i>


00:49:38.323 --> 00:49:40.193
<i>the authors of their own misery</i>


00:49:40.225 --> 00:49:43.363
<i>and success can only be a matter
of winning versus losing.</i>


00:49:43.396 --> 00:49:47.167
<i>Since the vast majority will no doubt
lose, they live vicariously.</i>


00:49:47.200 --> 00:49:50.236
<i>If their sports team wins
the game, so do they.</i>


00:49:50.269 --> 00:49:51.805
<i>If their country goes to war,</i>


00:49:51.838 --> 00:49:54.339
<i>they wave their flags
as if they were at war.</i>


00:49:54.372 --> 00:49:56.508
<i>While following
their celebrity heroes,</i>


00:49:56.542 --> 00:50:00.080
<i>feeling as though somehow
that success mirrors their own.</i>


00:50:00.113 --> 00:50:02.682
<i>And when that doesn't
work, they move inward,</i>


00:50:02.714 --> 00:50:07.287
<i>seeking self-help retreats,
therapy, medication, illicit drugs.</i>


00:50:07.319 --> 00:50:09.354
Anything to avoid
the identity crisis.


00:50:11.624 --> 00:50:14.593
That the society they mirror
just might be deeply flawed.


00:50:15.794 --> 00:50:17.729
So the masses remain complacent,


00:50:17.763 --> 00:50:20.266
short-sighted, bigoted,


00:50:20.298 --> 00:50:22.301
primitive, delusional.


00:50:23.202 --> 00:50:24.104
Manageable.


00:50:28.240 --> 00:50:30.476
No conspiracy required.


00:50:31.510 --> 00:50:34.446
Viable systems
regulate themselves.


00:50:34.479 --> 00:50:37.684
Viable?
You see all this as sustainable.


00:50:38.618 --> 00:50:41.287
<i>No conspiracy required.</i>


00:50:41.319 --> 00:50:44.423
- <i>Viable systems regulate them...</i>
- We just picked up the signal.


00:50:48.693 --> 00:50:52.798
Now there's one thing you missed
in your monologue there.


00:50:54.834 --> 00:50:58.571
Aside from primal provocation,
keeping people half-conscious,


00:50:58.604 --> 00:51:01.774
trapped in lower brain
fight or flight mode.


00:51:01.807 --> 00:51:04.711
Aside from the cultural hegemony
where people's values


00:51:04.743 --> 00:51:08.548
and envies mirror
those of wealth and power,


00:51:08.580 --> 00:51:10.550
reinforcing social order.


00:51:11.684 --> 00:51:14.553
And aside
from the climate of opinion


00:51:14.586 --> 00:51:17.723
fostered by the acclaimed
intelligentsia


00:51:17.756 --> 00:51:21.360
deciding the limits
by which truth must conform


00:51:21.394 --> 00:51:23.796
the most critical mechanism here


00:51:23.828 --> 00:51:26.533
is that of social inclusion.


00:51:26.566 --> 00:51:29.368
Nature wired us
with a strong tendency


00:51:29.401 --> 00:51:32.638
to override rational thought
in favor of group acceptance.


00:51:32.671 --> 00:51:35.307
Part of our evolutionary
fitness.


00:51:35.341 --> 00:51:37.911
And when people
violate consensus


00:51:37.943 --> 00:51:40.612
the nervous system seeks
to correct the behavior


00:51:40.646 --> 00:51:43.249
with pain and fear,
as there's little more


00:51:43.281 --> 00:51:47.254
psychologically damaging
than social exclusion.


00:51:49.222 --> 00:51:51.890
To be ostracized.
Ridicule, stigma,


00:51:51.923 --> 00:51:55.727
loss of reputation which could
also mean loss of employment,


00:51:55.760 --> 00:51:58.297
income, lost and survival.


00:51:58.330 --> 00:52:01.200
Yet there's a long history of people
who have moved against that tendency.


00:52:01.234 --> 00:52:03.569
A long history
of very few people


00:52:03.602 --> 00:52:06.572
who inevitably turn
into mere righteous symbols


00:52:06.606 --> 00:52:09.508
put on T-shirts rather
than forces of revolution.


00:52:09.542 --> 00:52:12.511
So this Orion problem of yours
isn't indicative of anything?


00:52:12.544 --> 00:52:15.747
Orion appears to be
a fringe group of extremists


00:52:15.781 --> 00:52:18.318
with no public support.


00:52:18.350 --> 00:52:23.256
This is about normative culture,
and my point, John,


00:52:24.256 --> 00:52:26.892
is that given our social nature,


00:52:26.926 --> 00:52:30.597
the stronger force here
is not on the side of reason,


00:52:30.629 --> 00:52:34.566
it's on the side of inclusion
and conformity,


00:52:34.600 --> 00:52:39.739
and that, my friend, is the
greatest form of social control


00:52:39.772 --> 00:52:42.575
and why the masses
will never break out


00:52:42.607 --> 00:52:45.412
of its self-perpetuated
oppression.


00:55:23.868 --> 00:55:25.905
<i>♪ Twenty-three I see
come with me my dear ♪</i>


00:55:25.937 --> 00:55:28.474
<i>♪ It's time we re-examine
this reality ♪</i>


00:56:36.175 --> 00:56:37.810
<i>♪ Be ready ♪</i>


00:56:37.843 --> 00:56:41.948
<i>♪ Welcome
to the Freakshow, baby ♪</i>


00:56:41.981 --> 00:56:45.118
<i>♪ This is what it is ♪</i>


00:57:12.211 --> 00:57:14.613
<i>♪ So you see, 23 ♪</i>


00:57:42.841 --> 00:57:44.777
<i>♪ And the cast
is currently stocked ♪</i>


00:57:44.810 --> 00:57:46.746
<i>♪ But we'll let you know
if we need another floor ♪</i>


00:57:46.778 --> 00:57:48.146
<i>♪ To be mopped ♪</i>


00:57:55.754 --> 00:57:58.190
So earlier something
was said to the effect


00:57:58.222 --> 00:58:00.258
that humans
are not designed to exist


00:58:00.292 --> 00:58:03.896
in an economically
stratified society.


00:58:03.928 --> 00:58:05.764
So to speak, yes.


00:58:05.798 --> 00:58:09.001
A stratified society is far
more unhealthy and unstable


00:58:09.033 --> 00:58:11.136
when compared
to an egalitarian one.


00:58:11.169 --> 00:58:13.673
That seems like
a pretty bold conclusion.


00:58:13.705 --> 00:58:16.341
- Can you elaborate?
- Sure.


00:58:16.374 --> 00:58:20.312
Consider our biology,
specifically the human brain.


00:58:20.345 --> 00:58:23.114
We're profoundly wired
for social response.


00:58:23.147 --> 00:58:25.885
For instance, the same
brain centers that react


00:58:25.917 --> 00:58:28.887
to physical pain also
react to emotional pain,


00:58:28.921 --> 00:58:32.692
such as feeling rejected,
excluded or shamed.


00:58:32.725 --> 00:58:35.328
In early life,
socially isolated infants,


00:58:35.361 --> 00:58:37.597
not receiving proper
affection will fail


00:58:37.629 --> 00:58:39.832
to produce critical
growth hormones,


00:58:39.865 --> 00:58:41.334
harming development.


00:58:41.367 --> 00:58:44.703
While in adulthood
similar effects occur.


00:58:44.736 --> 00:58:48.006
For example, there were
these dehumanizing institutions


00:58:48.039 --> 00:58:50.075
called prisons
and they practiced


00:58:50.109 --> 00:58:53.613
solitary confinement,
severe social isolation,


00:58:53.646 --> 00:58:56.281
and that practice literally
caused brain damage.


00:58:57.249 --> 00:58:59.919
Now, what do these
examples have in common?


00:58:59.952 --> 00:59:03.923
They are negative responses
to social related stress.


00:59:03.955 --> 00:59:06.057
And when you review
the past 200 years,


00:59:06.091 --> 00:59:08.694
of epidemiological study
on the issue,


00:59:08.727 --> 00:59:11.763
you realize that an economically
stratified society


00:59:11.796 --> 00:59:14.399
is one of the most toxically
stressful conditions


00:59:14.432 --> 00:59:17.135
you could ever impose
upon the human species.


00:59:18.037 --> 00:59:20.740
We've all learned about
the horrors of abject poverty.


00:59:20.772 --> 00:59:22.374
A condition that
affected a billion people


00:59:22.408 --> 00:59:24.377
at the turn of the 21st century,


00:59:24.410 --> 00:59:27.178
causing literally millions
of deaths each year.


00:59:27.211 --> 00:59:30.248
But the negative effects
of economic stratification


00:59:30.281 --> 00:59:32.251
aren't limited
to the distinctly poor.


00:59:32.283 --> 00:59:34.720
Inequality harms
just about everyone.


00:59:34.752 --> 00:59:38.124
A kind of social pollution and
the lower one finds themselves


00:59:38.156 --> 00:59:42.060
on the stratified ladder,
the worse their health becomes on average.


00:59:42.093 --> 00:59:43.963
Consider a lower class mother


00:59:43.995 --> 00:59:47.432
working two jobs, in debt,
can't afford a car,


00:59:47.466 --> 00:59:49.734
living paycheck to paycheck


00:59:49.767 --> 00:59:52.003
while trying to take care
of her young child.


00:59:52.037 --> 00:59:54.839
They may not be homeless,
starving or even poor


00:59:54.872 --> 00:59:56.274
by legal standards,


00:59:56.307 --> 00:59:57.842
but every day is still


00:59:57.876 --> 00:59:59.778
a battle to make ends meet.


00:59:59.812 --> 01:00:03.249
This is known as relative
poverty or more formally


01:00:03.281 --> 01:00:06.051
low socioeconomic status.


01:00:06.084 --> 01:00:09.054
And a defining characteristic
of this condition


01:00:09.088 --> 01:00:12.357
on average
is high psychosocial stress,


01:00:12.390 --> 01:00:15.026
meaning stress related
to social factors.


01:00:15.060 --> 01:00:18.764
This stress includes not only
feelings of general insecurity,


01:00:18.796 --> 01:00:20.800
such as worrying
about paying your bills,


01:00:20.832 --> 01:00:24.869
affording your child's next
doctor visit or losing your job,


01:00:24.903 --> 01:00:27.906
but also the stress
of social status itself.


01:00:27.939 --> 01:00:31.743
How one feels about themselves
compared to others.


01:00:31.776 --> 01:00:34.412
And while that particular
aspect may seem trivial,


01:00:34.446 --> 01:00:37.415
the fact is our brains
have evolved to react


01:00:37.448 --> 01:00:39.885
in profoundly specific
ways when it comes


01:00:39.917 --> 01:00:42.354
to how we think others see us.


01:00:42.386 --> 01:00:46.859
We have an acute sensitivity
to our perceived social status.


01:00:46.892 --> 01:00:48.894
In other words,
it's not just about the stress


01:00:48.926 --> 01:00:51.062
of endless worry
and the technical difficulty


01:00:51.095 --> 01:00:53.231
of being poor that's toxic.


01:00:53.265 --> 01:00:56.969
It's equally if not more about
the stress of feeling poor.


01:00:57.002 --> 01:01:00.272
For example, studies have shown
if you take people with the same


01:01:00.305 --> 01:01:01.874
equal access
to free health care,


01:01:01.906 --> 01:01:03.876
controlling
for lifestyle factors,


01:01:03.908 --> 01:01:05.877
you will still see,
as you inch down


01:01:05.910 --> 01:01:08.347
the ladder of income and wealth,
people's health getting


01:01:08.379 --> 01:01:10.816
progressively worse on average.


01:01:10.848 --> 01:01:13.051
The lower they are
in the class hierarchy


01:01:13.084 --> 01:01:15.220
the sicker they become.


01:01:15.254 --> 01:01:16.856
One mechanism for this


01:01:16.888 --> 01:01:18.890
is that high
psychological stress


01:01:18.923 --> 01:01:21.259
leads to a state
of chronic inflammation


01:01:21.292 --> 01:01:24.497
and what's called
an allostatic overload.


01:01:24.530 --> 01:01:27.932
Allostasis means your body's
trying to recover from something


01:01:27.966 --> 01:01:30.502
working to return
to a more balanced state.


01:01:30.535 --> 01:01:32.470
But it can't. And this causes


01:01:32.504 --> 01:01:35.473
the body and the mind
to wear down rapidly.


01:01:35.506 --> 01:01:39.278
Living in relative poverty
in all its day-to-day insecurity


01:01:39.310 --> 01:01:41.446
and feelings of low self-worth,


01:01:41.479 --> 01:01:45.150
keeps people psychologically
locked in a stressful state.


01:01:45.184 --> 01:01:48.120
Ravaging mental
and physical health.


01:01:48.153 --> 01:01:51.290
<i>Consider heart disease.
low socioeconomic status</i>


01:01:51.323 --> 01:01:54.460
<i>creates a 50% greater chance
of its development.</i>


01:01:54.493 --> 01:01:57.463
<i>and not just because people
may have poor lifestyle habits,</i>


01:01:57.495 --> 01:02:00.398
<i>but due to psychosocial
stress itself,</i>


01:02:00.432 --> 01:02:03.502
<i>which increases the hormone
cortisol, damaging arteries</i>


01:02:03.535 --> 01:02:06.172
<i>fostering strokes
and heart attacks.</i>


01:02:06.205 --> 01:02:09.408
<i>Low socioeconomic status
is a heart disease risk factor</i>


01:02:09.441 --> 01:02:12.977
<i>on its own,
similar for diabetes and cancer</i>


01:02:13.010 --> 01:02:16.080
<i>with far higher rates
for those relatively poor.</i>


01:02:16.113 --> 01:02:20.586
<i>As one study put it,
"Poverty itself is a carcinogen."</i>


01:02:20.618 --> 01:02:23.222
And given that heart disease
diabetes and cancer


01:02:23.254 --> 01:02:26.090
were some of the leading causes
of death in that highly unequal


01:02:26.124 --> 01:02:28.560
global society
of the early 21st century,


01:02:28.593 --> 01:02:31.563
these facts help explain
why life span gaps


01:02:31.597 --> 01:02:34.399
between the rich and the poor
were shockingly wide.


01:02:34.432 --> 01:02:38.203
Ranging from 15 to 40 years
depending on region.


01:02:38.236 --> 01:02:39.972
And then you have mental health.


01:02:40.004 --> 01:02:43.341
Low socioeconomic status
fuels much higher instances


01:02:43.374 --> 01:02:45.877
of depression,
anxiety disorders,


01:02:45.910 --> 01:02:48.146
schizophrenia, suicide,


01:02:48.180 --> 01:02:51.417
not to mention violence,
including child abuse.


01:02:51.450 --> 01:02:53.953
The condition of poverty
was found to be the leading


01:02:53.986 --> 01:02:57.256
predictor of child abuse,
which is particularly troubling


01:02:57.289 --> 01:03:00.292
since such abuse often
leads to adult disorders


01:03:00.325 --> 01:03:03.229
such as addictions,
antisocial behavior,


01:03:03.261 --> 01:03:07.066
immune system problems,
cognitive impairment.


01:03:07.098 --> 01:03:09.401
In fact, it was found
that children simply living


01:03:09.434 --> 01:03:12.504
in the condition of poverty
correlated to large decreases


01:03:12.537 --> 01:03:15.241
in IQ,
decreased brain development,


01:03:15.274 --> 01:03:17.877
and worst overall, health
throughout the life cycle.


01:03:17.910 --> 01:03:19.578
Personally, I would argue that


01:03:19.611 --> 01:03:22.314
if child abuse is
about negligence and harm,


01:03:22.347 --> 01:03:25.651
any society that tolerates
the existence of poverty


01:03:25.684 --> 01:03:27.886
when it has the means to end it,


01:03:27.919 --> 01:03:30.889
is a society that is
fundamentally abusive to children.


01:03:32.457 --> 01:03:37.328
Now, as far as behavioral violence
in general, it's no surprise.


01:03:37.361 --> 01:03:40.298
The pre-transition period
was saturated in it.


01:03:40.332 --> 01:03:44.103
The emotional pathogen behind
most acts of violence is shame


01:03:44.135 --> 01:03:48.106
and inequality produces shame
like a finely tuned machine.


01:03:48.140 --> 01:03:51.343
Shootings, gang violence,
terrorism,


01:03:51.376 --> 01:03:55.214
domestic violence, all highly
correlated to inequality,


01:03:55.247 --> 01:03:58.584
like a toxic cloud hovering
over civilization.


01:03:58.617 --> 01:04:01.153
The more economically
unequal a society,


01:04:01.185 --> 01:04:03.555
the more violent it tended
to be on average.


01:04:03.588 --> 01:04:07.926
And that goes for most everything in
terms of negative public health outcomes.


01:04:07.959 --> 01:04:11.463
With higher incidences
of disease, crime, obesity,


01:04:11.495 --> 01:04:15.233
infant mortality, homicides,
teen birth, mental illness,


01:04:15.267 --> 01:04:18.069
poor education, conflict,
domestic abuse,


01:04:18.102 --> 01:04:20.972
illiteracy, suicide,
premature mortality,


01:04:21.006 --> 01:04:24.310
overall mistrust and much more.


01:04:25.310 --> 01:04:29.615
There is no viable defense
of its existence on any level


01:04:29.647 --> 01:04:31.383
and it's certainly
not representative


01:04:31.415 --> 01:04:33.519
of a fixed human nature.


01:04:33.551 --> 01:04:37.622
Humans are basically allergic to
socio-economic stratification.


01:06:52.124 --> 01:06:54.158
What are you doing? Come on!


01:09:53.738 --> 01:09:56.441
So how's this supposed
to happen exactly?


01:09:56.473 --> 01:09:57.943
I'm not sure.


01:09:57.976 --> 01:10:00.979
The satellite details
we need are very specific.


01:10:01.012 --> 01:10:04.383
How John pulls this off
is going to be interesting.


01:10:07.819 --> 01:10:10.022
Hey, where did
you get the popcorn?


01:10:10.055 --> 01:10:11.890
Oh, I don't know.
It was just here.


01:10:14.391 --> 01:10:15.560
Right.


01:10:17.329 --> 01:10:19.331
Are they still in debate mode?


01:10:19.364 --> 01:10:20.499
Listen for yourself.


01:10:24.002 --> 01:10:25.971
Hope you went to college.


01:10:26.003 --> 01:10:28.707
...and why the masses
will never break out


01:10:28.739 --> 01:10:31.876
of its self-perpetuated
oppression.


01:10:33.677 --> 01:10:37.481
Historically observable.
Biologically sound.


01:10:37.515 --> 01:10:39.618
And grossly exaggerated.


01:10:39.650 --> 01:10:43.020
While most may indeed be stuck in
lower brain, limbic system reflexes,


01:10:43.053 --> 01:10:45.824
you underestimate
the prefrontal cortex.


01:10:45.856 --> 01:10:48.493
Our ability to transcend
primitive reactions.


01:10:48.525 --> 01:10:50.461
Whether you believe it
or not, Simon,


01:10:50.494 --> 01:10:52.997
the activists of the world
are slowly becoming more aware,


01:10:53.030 --> 01:10:56.435
- more focused.
- Focused on what?


01:10:56.467 --> 01:10:57.868
The system?


01:10:57.901 --> 01:10:59.937
The origin of the social
psychology that keeps


01:10:59.971 --> 01:11:01.640
those feedback loops
of oppression going.


01:11:03.475 --> 01:11:06.544
Ah, so threat to the money God?


01:11:07.579 --> 01:11:09.381
If you want to be
spooky about it, sure.


01:11:10.147 --> 01:11:13.385
The money God is eventually
going to be overthrown.


01:11:13.418 --> 01:11:15.387
This age-old march
toward increased the quality


01:11:15.419 --> 01:11:17.989
and human rights is now
accelerating into new territory.


01:11:19.056 --> 01:11:21.525
And one way or another it's
eventually going to arrive


01:11:21.559 --> 01:11:23.729
at the doorstep of the economy.


01:11:23.762 --> 01:11:25.497
And then what?


01:11:25.529 --> 01:11:28.833
You seem to be suffering
from a kind of amnesia, John.


01:11:28.867 --> 01:11:30.901
That moment's long past.


01:11:30.935 --> 01:11:34.439
Immortalized by the failed
Soviet experiment,


01:11:34.471 --> 01:11:36.941
a memory that's fostered
an enduring boogeyman.


01:11:38.943 --> 01:11:43.382
Anyone today daring
to suggest economic equality,


01:11:43.414 --> 01:11:45.684
which is what I assume
you are getting at,


01:11:45.717 --> 01:11:48.820
as some final stage
of human rights progress,


01:11:48.852 --> 01:11:52.490
will quickly be condemned
as a freedom-hating socialist.


01:11:52.524 --> 01:11:56.528
Propaganda may be strong,
but so are the mounting problems,


01:11:56.561 --> 01:11:58.964
problems that have
no in system solution,


01:11:58.997 --> 01:12:02.401
- forcing people to think differently.
- Such as?


01:12:02.434 --> 01:12:04.569
How about the collective insult
that one percent of the world's


01:12:04.601 --> 01:12:07.138
population now owns
80% of the wealth?


01:12:07.172 --> 01:12:10.008
Or more importantly,
that every life support system


01:12:10.040 --> 01:12:14.078
continues to be in decline
with now millions dislocated.


01:12:14.111 --> 01:12:16.914
Famines, wars, growing poverty.


01:12:16.948 --> 01:12:20.718
People will eventually realize the
economic mechanisms behind this.


01:12:20.752 --> 01:12:24.823
Further opening the gate.
Same for technological unemployment.


01:12:24.855 --> 01:12:27.591
Half of all jobs have
already been automated.


01:12:27.624 --> 01:12:30.694
And while nations have compensated
by giving basic income,


01:12:30.727 --> 01:12:32.730
the system contradiction
is still clear.


01:12:32.763 --> 01:12:35.534
What happens when people realize
this welfare program is really


01:12:35.566 --> 01:12:38.803
just an excuse to keep
the labor system in place?


01:12:38.837 --> 01:12:41.406
Hence keeping
the ruling class in place.


01:12:42.640 --> 01:12:44.676
You assume too much, John.


01:12:44.708 --> 01:12:46.944
Three-quarters of the people
on that planet,


01:12:46.977 --> 01:12:50.214
believe in supernatural
beings that live in the sky


01:12:50.248 --> 01:12:52.217
affecting their lives.


01:12:52.249 --> 01:12:54.586
You're projecting
your rare intelligence


01:12:54.619 --> 01:12:57.155
upon a sea of glorified savages.


01:12:57.187 --> 01:13:00.191
And if you think the activist
community has anything


01:13:00.225 --> 01:13:04.596
in their toolkit to even
approach system level change,


01:13:04.628 --> 01:13:06.864
you're not paying attention
to their ignorance.


01:13:06.897 --> 01:13:08.867
You mean the spectacle?


01:13:08.900 --> 01:13:10.969
People piling
into free speech zones,


01:13:11.002 --> 01:13:13.205
holding up signs,
yelling at buildings,


01:13:13.238 --> 01:13:16.708
ranting on social media,
creating political art,


01:13:16.740 --> 01:13:18.810
poetry, writing books...


01:13:20.211 --> 01:13:22.079
making movies.


01:13:22.113 --> 01:13:23.815
I agree it's mostly catharsis.


01:13:23.847 --> 01:13:25.749
It's a pressure release valve,


01:13:25.783 --> 01:13:27.718
easing periodic tension,


01:13:27.752 --> 01:13:30.589
making people feel like they're
actually doing something.


01:13:31.623 --> 01:13:34.559
Aside, of course,
from helping the economy,


01:13:34.592 --> 01:13:35.994
the anti-establishment market


01:13:36.026 --> 01:13:37.828
has been increasingly
profitable.


01:13:37.861 --> 01:13:40.498
Yes.


01:13:40.531 --> 01:13:42.934
The anger dollar.
If only such outrage


01:13:42.967 --> 01:13:45.036
could be packaged and traded
on Wall Street, right?


01:13:45.069 --> 01:13:49.607
And then social
change might have a chance.


01:13:59.150 --> 01:14:03.989
But catharsis aside, John,
the real issue is hope.


01:14:04.021 --> 01:14:07.225
Activism today
is a hope industry.


01:14:08.258 --> 01:14:10.928
Take Concordia.
It's been irritating


01:14:10.962 --> 01:14:13.698
and I'm certainly bothered
by the technology you have,


01:14:13.730 --> 01:14:16.834
but your actions have posed
no true threat.


01:14:16.868 --> 01:14:21.006
What you do is give
your millions of fans hope.


01:14:21.038 --> 01:14:24.575
And hope is a drug that subdues.


01:14:24.609 --> 01:14:27.579
So the long history of rights
progress is meaningless?


01:14:27.611 --> 01:14:30.915
The abolition of slavery,
women's liberation,


01:14:30.949 --> 01:14:35.053
child labor laws, unions,
indigenous restitution,


01:14:35.086 --> 01:14:39.925
global decrees, LGBTQ equality,
disability acts?


01:14:39.958 --> 01:14:42.727
All adaptations
and accommodations.


01:14:42.760 --> 01:14:45.129
No threat to the system itself.


01:14:45.163 --> 01:14:47.098
Take abject slavery:


01:14:47.131 --> 01:14:48.800
the origins are clear.


01:14:48.833 --> 01:14:50.869
It was never about racism.


01:14:50.901 --> 01:14:52.570
It was about economic
exploitation.


01:14:52.604 --> 01:14:54.806
Hence business as usual.


01:14:54.838 --> 01:14:57.274
And yet racism took the heat.


01:14:57.307 --> 01:15:00.078
The system connection
goes unrecognized.


01:15:00.110 --> 01:15:02.279
Limits of debate.
People have been conditioned


01:15:02.312 --> 01:15:04.882
to seek moral causes
rather than structural ones.


01:15:04.915 --> 01:15:08.820
Which is exactly my point,
they don't have the vocabulary.


01:15:08.852 --> 01:15:10.955
Nothing
in their experience offers it.


01:15:10.989 --> 01:15:14.125
The average person engages
six hours of media a day


01:15:14.158 --> 01:15:17.227
much of that news constantly
reinforcing the status quo.


01:15:17.261 --> 01:15:21.098
I'm glad you brought that up.
News is a business.


01:15:21.132 --> 01:15:24.269
And do you think that any
for-profit institution is ever


01:15:24.302 --> 01:15:28.106
going to tolerate ideas that
move against how it survives?


01:15:29.806 --> 01:15:31.876
The odds are stacked, John.


01:15:31.909 --> 01:15:34.779
The system protects
itself on every level


01:15:34.811 --> 01:15:37.582
almost as if it were
a living organism.


01:15:39.249 --> 01:15:42.119
But for argument's sake,


01:15:42.153 --> 01:15:45.690
let's assume a formidable
movement existed.


01:15:45.722 --> 01:15:48.859
A united front to change
the social structure.


01:15:48.892 --> 01:15:50.160
Then what?


01:15:50.194 --> 01:15:51.930
Does it play out on the stage


01:15:51.962 --> 01:15:53.397
of political theater?


01:15:53.431 --> 01:15:56.868
A stage owned and operated
by business power?


01:15:56.900 --> 01:16:00.037
Part of the awakening. People are
realizing their elected officials


01:16:00.070 --> 01:16:02.239
are structurally
corrupted by default,


01:16:02.272 --> 01:16:03.941
regardless of intent.


01:16:03.975 --> 01:16:06.311
- Approaches will shift.
- To what?


01:16:06.343 --> 01:16:09.279
Insurrection, violence,
overthrow?


01:16:09.312 --> 01:16:11.048
A French Revolution?


01:16:11.082 --> 01:16:13.017
Possible,
but certainly not inevitable.


01:16:13.051 --> 01:16:14.919
A critical mass large
enough to stop


01:16:14.952 --> 01:16:16.855
the machine in its tracks is
really all that it's needed.


01:16:16.887 --> 01:16:18.390
You remember George Orwell?


01:16:18.422 --> 01:16:20.791
- Of course.
- He observed something


01:16:20.824 --> 01:16:22.860
interesting
in this endless battle


01:16:22.894 --> 01:16:26.131
between the haves
and the have nots.


01:16:26.163 --> 01:16:27.965
If it's true as you say,


01:16:27.998 --> 01:16:30.801
the masses are beginning
to understand the system.


01:16:30.834 --> 01:16:32.203
Building force against it.


01:16:32.235 --> 01:16:34.439
You should also recognize


01:16:34.471 --> 01:16:36.874
that there's a natural
counter-movement.


01:16:36.908 --> 01:16:39.778
The system defending
itself once again.


01:16:40.477 --> 01:16:42.913
And every threat
to its integrity,


01:16:42.946 --> 01:16:45.115
what you see as progress,


01:16:45.149 --> 01:16:47.986
will be twisted around
and presented to the public


01:16:48.019 --> 01:16:50.388
as an attack
on their way of life.


01:16:51.722 --> 01:16:54.158
Those outliers
that you spoke of,


01:16:54.191 --> 01:16:57.428
the terrorists, gangs,
criminals, mass murderers,


01:16:57.462 --> 01:17:00.932
insurgencies, hackers,
the Orions.


01:17:00.964 --> 01:17:02.934
The Concordias.


01:17:02.967 --> 01:17:05.970
All empower
the system in the end


01:17:06.003 --> 01:17:09.374
providing excuses
to further tighten things down.


01:17:09.406 --> 01:17:11.943
More police, more prisons,


01:17:11.976 --> 01:17:15.080
more laws, more bombs,
more surveillance.


01:17:16.180 --> 01:17:17.883
More control.


01:17:19.249 --> 01:17:23.954
Again, no conspiracy required.


01:17:24.855 --> 01:17:28.126
It's the masses themselves
that push for this,


01:17:28.159 --> 01:17:31.263
willfully exchanging
their freedom for security.


01:17:32.195 --> 01:17:37.034
So they can comfortably
return to their workstations


01:17:37.068 --> 01:17:41.172
and continue pulling
levers on the machine


01:17:41.204 --> 01:17:44.742
just as a money God ordained.


01:21:36.039 --> 01:21:38.342
In the end,
it wasn't the so-called communist,


01:21:38.376 --> 01:21:41.412
socialists, anarchists or
whatever counterculture group


01:21:41.445 --> 01:21:45.049
that posed the most serious
argument for the Great Transition.


01:21:45.082 --> 01:21:47.084
It was the environmental
scientist.


01:21:47.118 --> 01:21:49.454
One could debate
the ins and outs of morality,


01:21:49.486 --> 01:21:51.388
public health and human rights,


01:21:51.422 --> 01:21:54.726
but if the habitat goes
all that becomes moot.


01:21:54.758 --> 01:21:56.627
And at the turn
of the 21st century


01:21:56.659 --> 01:22:00.464
our ecological negligence
was pretty embarrassing.


01:22:00.498 --> 01:22:02.266
With great inefficiency
we were using


01:22:02.298 --> 01:22:04.435
far more resources each year


01:22:04.467 --> 01:22:06.269
than the planet produced.


01:22:06.302 --> 01:22:08.739
Had destroyed vast realms
of biodiversity,


01:22:08.772 --> 01:22:11.743
polluted the air, the soil,
the water,


01:22:11.775 --> 01:22:14.745
not only destabilizing
the entire global ecosystem


01:22:14.779 --> 01:22:18.016
but by extension society itself.


01:22:18.048 --> 01:22:22.352
The most common question I get
when teaching this history is,


01:22:22.386 --> 01:22:25.656
"How is it even possible
things could get so bad?


01:22:25.689 --> 01:22:28.226
How could everyone just keep
blindly pulling levers


01:22:28.258 --> 01:22:30.328
on that destructive
economic machine


01:22:30.360 --> 01:22:32.296
and not see what was happening?"


01:22:32.329 --> 01:22:36.100
And it comes down to a kind
of faith-based conditioning,


01:22:36.132 --> 01:22:38.101
a religious pathology
taking the form


01:22:38.135 --> 01:22:40.104
of mass economic behavior.


01:22:40.137 --> 01:22:43.674
The doctrine was
that of universal scarcity.


01:22:43.707 --> 01:22:46.276
People had been taught
to believe that at no time,


01:22:46.310 --> 01:22:49.614
under no circumstance,
can economic balance exist.


01:22:49.646 --> 01:22:52.816
The very idea an
economy could be organized


01:22:52.850 --> 01:22:56.287
to efficiently provide
for everyone while also being


01:22:56.320 --> 01:23:00.058
in balance with the habitat
was a sacrilegious taboo.


01:23:00.091 --> 01:23:03.127
The cult of scarcity and
consumption wasn't having it.


01:23:03.159 --> 01:23:05.229
They considered it
utopian thinking.


01:23:05.262 --> 01:23:08.166
Supporting the myth
that people had infinite wants


01:23:08.199 --> 01:23:11.102
and were accusatively
insatiable.


01:23:11.135 --> 01:23:14.439
Hence, the poor had to exist
and if anything was the problem,


01:23:14.471 --> 01:23:17.307
it must be population
not the system.


01:23:18.275 --> 01:23:22.580
That was the prevailing dogma.
There must be too many people.


01:23:22.613 --> 01:23:25.182
You can't have ecological
balance in a system


01:23:25.216 --> 01:23:28.285
that requires constant
consumer activity to work.


01:23:28.319 --> 01:23:30.521
It's one thing to consume
based on need.


01:23:30.553 --> 01:23:33.790
It's another to consume
because the system demands it.


01:23:33.824 --> 01:23:35.860
And the market system
of economics needed


01:23:35.892 --> 01:23:39.129
constant turnover of goods
to keep and create jobs,


01:23:39.163 --> 01:23:42.100
providing workers, which
of course were also consumers,


01:23:42.132 --> 01:23:44.668
with income to spend back
into the system,


01:23:44.702 --> 01:23:48.106
endlessly repeating the cycle
of cyclical consumption.


01:23:48.138 --> 01:23:50.240
If it didn't repeat
fast enough or slowed,


01:23:50.274 --> 01:23:51.776
the economy contracted.


01:23:51.809 --> 01:23:53.845
Purchasing power
wasn't circulating


01:23:53.878 --> 01:23:56.681
and the society
proceeded to shut down.


01:23:56.713 --> 01:24:00.618
A very unique historical
moment occurred in the early 20th century


01:24:00.650 --> 01:24:05.288
when it was realized that technology
was now creating a good surplus


01:24:05.321 --> 01:24:07.658
and great confusion ensued.


01:24:07.690 --> 01:24:10.794
The problem was this newfound
productive efficiency


01:24:10.828 --> 01:24:13.698
was not being met by people
buying more stuff.


01:24:13.730 --> 01:24:16.133
So two competing
perspectives emerged:


01:24:16.167 --> 01:24:19.770
on one side you had idealists,
envisioning a new era.


01:24:19.802 --> 01:24:22.573
If we can produce
an overall good surplus,


01:24:22.605 --> 01:24:25.575
why not lower the cost
of goods respectively


01:24:25.609 --> 01:24:28.412
reducing work hours and
increased pay in proportion?


01:24:28.445 --> 01:24:31.883
So you can now have say a person
working only two days a week


01:24:31.915 --> 01:24:33.751
without losing
their standard of living


01:24:33.784 --> 01:24:36.454
since the market value
of labor and goods adjusted


01:24:36.486 --> 01:24:38.655
to compensate
for the increased efficiency.


01:24:38.689 --> 01:24:40.857
This logic makes perfect
sense when it comes


01:24:40.891 --> 01:24:43.628
to the basic principle
of supply and demand.


01:24:43.660 --> 01:24:46.864
Suddenly people have more
free time, not buried in debt.


01:24:46.896 --> 01:24:49.633
They can enrich their social
life, family life,


01:24:49.667 --> 01:24:51.703
and pursue the things
that have true meaning.


01:24:52.703 --> 01:24:55.740
Well, that's not
the way it played out


01:24:55.772 --> 01:24:57.542
nor would it ever.


01:24:57.574 --> 01:25:00.544
Which brings us to
the system level perspective


01:25:00.578 --> 01:25:03.614
since the system itself simply
isn't designed inherently


01:25:03.646 --> 01:25:05.783
for steady state equilibrium.


01:25:05.815 --> 01:25:09.519
Market economics is predicated
on a more is better ethic.


01:25:09.552 --> 01:25:11.588
To be competitive in the quest
for market share.


01:25:11.622 --> 01:25:13.658
That's what's incentivized.


01:25:13.690 --> 01:25:16.394
More growth, more sales,
more employees,


01:25:16.427 --> 01:25:21.299
more capital accumulation,
more profit, constant expansion.


01:25:21.332 --> 01:25:23.434
So what happened
was to be expected,


01:25:23.467 --> 01:25:24.969
fortifying a new industry,


01:25:25.002 --> 01:25:26.803
commercial advertising.


01:25:26.837 --> 01:25:28.573
What was once
a simple media service,


01:25:28.605 --> 01:25:31.309
notifying people
of new goods they may need,


01:25:31.342 --> 01:25:34.679
turned into a powerful form
of manipulative propaganda.


01:25:34.712 --> 01:25:38.281
In the later stages, companies
spent more money on advertising


01:25:38.315 --> 01:25:40.751
than they did on research
and development.


01:25:40.784 --> 01:25:44.355
What advertising does is
abuse our social nature


01:25:44.387 --> 01:25:46.790
by making people feel
like they're missing out.


01:25:46.824 --> 01:25:48.726
They're not good
enough without this,


01:25:48.758 --> 01:25:50.962
they're lower in status
without that.


01:25:50.994 --> 01:25:54.731
They feel excluded from others
if they don't own something.


01:25:54.765 --> 01:25:57.235
And as pathetic as
all that sounds it had


01:25:57.267 --> 01:26:00.704
a profound effect on society
with everyone keeping up


01:26:00.738 --> 01:26:04.609
with the Joneses
in a hideous feedback loop.


01:26:04.641 --> 01:26:07.310
And the result
as industrial productivity


01:26:07.343 --> 01:26:10.748
still continued to rise,
people worked more than ever,


01:26:10.780 --> 01:26:13.984
