How contemporacist of you.


01:41:27.596 --> 01:41:31.233
Yet 20th century study of
numerous hunter-gatherer tribes,


01:41:31.266 --> 01:41:34.236
those still surviving in
remote areas just as they did


01:41:34.270 --> 01:41:36.806
thousands of years prior,
actually show socially


01:41:36.838 --> 01:41:40.943
rich cultures. Adult life
spans not far from ours.


01:41:40.976 --> 01:41:43.613
Relatively peaceful
in balance with nature.


01:41:43.645 --> 01:41:48.250
No leaders, no group hierarchy,
no inequality.


01:41:48.284 --> 01:41:52.422
To argue today's society is somehow
more civilized is dubious at best.


01:41:52.454 --> 01:41:54.658
Well, then perhaps
you can encourage


01:41:54.690 --> 01:41:56.559
all your enlightened followers


01:41:56.592 --> 01:41:58.861
to come together
and live out their utopian


01:41:58.895 --> 01:42:00.797
fantasy in the Amazon jungle.


01:42:00.829 --> 01:42:03.533
You mean what's left of it?
What hasn't been destroyed


01:42:03.565 --> 01:42:05.769
by the supposedly advanced
culture that's ravaged


01:42:05.802 --> 01:42:07.938
the natural world
into total decline


01:42:07.971 --> 01:42:11.908
in the name of infinite
consumption and economic growth?


01:42:11.940 --> 01:42:14.743
And the point here, Simon,
is hunter-gatherer cultures


01:42:14.776 --> 01:42:16.879
are evidence of human
variability.


01:42:16.913 --> 01:42:19.982
variability which contradicts
your vague biological determinism.


01:42:20.016 --> 01:42:22.519
John, just because history shows


01:42:22.552 --> 01:42:25.922
a range of behaviors across
time doesn't prove anything.


01:42:25.954 --> 01:42:29.225
The introduction
of agriculture indeed changed


01:42:29.258 --> 01:42:33.462
the human condition because
it triggered a dormant trait


01:42:33.495 --> 01:42:35.899
in our evolutionary psychology.


01:42:35.931 --> 01:42:38.667
A trait that wasn't
expressed before.


01:42:38.700 --> 01:42:39.735
How?


01:42:39.769 --> 01:42:41.370
By the advent


01:42:41.404 --> 01:42:43.339
of economic surplus.


01:42:43.373 --> 01:42:44.941
Economic surplus.


01:42:44.973 --> 01:42:48.477
Resources and goods
that could be stored,


01:42:48.511 --> 01:42:50.946
hoarded, stockpiled, owned,


01:42:50.980 --> 01:42:54.618
traded, controlled,
leveraged for personal gain.


01:42:54.650 --> 01:42:58.988
A phenomenon that was impossible
in a hunter-gatherer reality.


01:42:59.021 --> 01:43:02.591
And it was that realization
that sparked our now


01:43:02.624 --> 01:43:05.995
omnipresent drive toward
dominance and hierarchy.


01:43:09.399 --> 01:43:10.367
I didn't know that.


01:43:11.368 --> 01:43:14.971
Genetic dormancy
of an evolutionary expression.


01:43:15.003 --> 01:43:17.406
Needed an environmental trigger,


01:43:17.440 --> 01:43:20.477
psychological drive,
but then morphs into complex


01:43:20.510 --> 01:43:22.878
oppressive institutions
and structures.


01:43:23.812 --> 01:43:27.484
Compelling. Intuitive.
Plausible.


01:43:28.918 --> 01:43:30.587
Too bad it's total bullshit.


01:43:30.619 --> 01:43:32.821
All simpleton, pedestrian,
bio-deterministic


01:43:32.855 --> 01:43:35.558
conclusions that are nothing
more than elitist projections.


01:43:35.591 --> 01:43:39.529
You think it's wise to insult me
given this circumstance, John.


01:43:40.596 --> 01:43:41.498
And listen.


01:44:12.494 --> 01:44:14.698
Agriculture did change
everything.


01:44:14.730 --> 01:44:16.899
But not because of someone's
dormant psychological


01:44:16.932 --> 01:44:19.836
drive magically triggered
by economic surplus.


01:44:19.869 --> 01:44:22.772
It was about what such a society
technically required,


01:44:22.805 --> 01:44:26.976
dramatically shifting incentives and
very nature of human relationships.


01:44:27.008 --> 01:44:30.346
Think about it.
First you need the proper land,


01:44:30.379 --> 01:44:32.548
water,
the right conditions to farm,


01:44:32.582 --> 01:44:34.651
then creating settlements
around those fruitful areas


01:44:34.684 --> 01:44:36.619
as opposed to foraging.


01:44:36.651 --> 01:44:39.588
And since land quality varies
some settlements will prosper


01:44:39.622 --> 01:44:42.459
due to their geography
and some will falter.


01:44:42.492 --> 01:44:44.961
So what happens when a group
finds itself with failed crops


01:44:44.994 --> 01:44:46.996
and no way
to survive the winter?


01:44:47.029 --> 01:44:48.598
They may trade
with other groups,


01:44:48.631 --> 01:44:50.600
building out
what we call a market today,


01:44:50.632 --> 01:44:53.669
giving way to the idea
of property and so on.


01:44:53.703 --> 01:44:55.839
Or if they have
nothing to trade, desperate,


01:44:55.872 --> 01:44:59.743
they may invade, they may steal,
compete,


01:44:59.775 --> 01:45:03.145
establishing the need
for protection, laws, armies,


01:45:03.178 --> 01:45:04.914
the state institution itself.


01:45:05.882 --> 01:45:08.518
At the same time people
begin to notice the imbalance


01:45:08.551 --> 01:45:10.887
and power
of this new propertied reality,


01:45:10.919 --> 01:45:14.524
rationalizing the hoarding of wealth
for the sake of future security.


01:45:15.425 --> 01:45:19.895
Hence the birth of inequity,
poverty, socio-economic class.


01:45:20.829 --> 01:45:24.900
Simon, every major structural
aspect of society today,


01:45:24.934 --> 01:45:27.971
from ownership to trade,
to nation states


01:45:28.003 --> 01:45:31.039
to institutional warfare
at the competitive ethic


01:45:31.073 --> 01:45:36.178
to vast economic inequality and
power hierarchy was predictable.


01:45:36.212 --> 01:45:37.647
Snowballing ever since.


01:45:38.814 --> 01:45:43.787
So your theory is if you change
the structure of society


01:45:43.820 --> 01:45:45.789
you change the human condition?


01:45:47.190 --> 01:45:50.693
- There's no going back, John.
- No one's going back.


01:45:50.726 --> 01:45:52.162
We're going forward.


01:45:52.195 --> 01:45:54.497
Humanity has been trapped
in this immature stage


01:45:54.529 --> 01:45:56.899
for too long, not to mention
the sickness manifest


01:45:56.932 --> 01:46:00.602
by this endless striving towards
social status is palpable.


01:46:00.636 --> 01:46:02.472
Children,
when who asked what they want


01:46:02.504 --> 01:46:06.074
to be when they grow up say,
"Rich and famous."


01:46:06.107 --> 01:46:08.977
How the most wealthy nations,
those beacons of supposed


01:46:09.011 --> 01:46:12.649
success are by far
the most mentally ill.


01:46:12.681 --> 01:46:16.218
People don't know who they are,
where they're going


01:46:16.252 --> 01:46:17.720
and what they're doing.


01:46:17.753 --> 01:46:19.990
Lost in a perversion
of social image.


01:46:20.890 --> 01:46:24.127
A spectacle that no longer
has any relationship


01:46:24.159 --> 01:46:25.595
to anything real.


01:50:39.914 --> 01:50:42.284
So I'd like to go back
to the subject of inequality.


01:50:42.318 --> 01:50:44.454
But this time
to understand the mechanics


01:50:44.486 --> 01:50:47.723
of the oppression how the
hierarchy was kept in place?


01:50:47.757 --> 01:50:49.726
Okay, let's start with money.


01:50:51.994 --> 01:50:54.831
Money was the infrastructure
of the market economy


01:50:54.864 --> 01:50:56.899
and how it was created
and moved around


01:50:56.931 --> 01:50:59.836
was instrumental
to lower class oppression.


01:50:59.869 --> 01:51:03.206
So you had these
things called banks and they had


01:51:03.239 --> 01:51:07.043
the ungodly power to make
abstract value out of nothing.


01:51:07.075 --> 01:51:11.046
If a person needed money
for a home or car or business,


01:51:11.079 --> 01:51:14.216
they went to their local bank
and applied for a loan,


01:51:14.249 --> 01:51:16.819
and if approved
the person signed a contract


01:51:16.851 --> 01:51:20.822
binding them to return that
loaned money at a future date.


01:51:20.855 --> 01:51:23.024
Though, it's not really a lone


01:51:23.057 --> 01:51:26.294
in the sense of somebody lending
out what they already owned.


01:51:26.328 --> 01:51:28.964
Contrary to what most assumed
banks didn't loan out money


01:51:28.998 --> 01:51:32.268
they actually had,
they instead created new money


01:51:32.301 --> 01:51:35.471
in the form of credit
backed by debt.


01:51:35.503 --> 01:51:37.973
So on one side money represented


01:51:38.007 --> 01:51:40.276
a store of value
people could spend,


01:51:40.309 --> 01:51:43.945
while on the other it was
a liability made out of debt.


01:51:43.979 --> 01:51:46.348
In other words,
for every dollar that existed,


01:51:46.382 --> 01:51:48.484
there was also
a debt of a dollar


01:51:48.516 --> 01:51:50.919
owed to some bank somewhere.


01:51:50.953 --> 01:51:53.289
That was how money was
brought into existence


01:51:53.321 --> 01:51:57.827
and when someone repaid the loan
debt the money then disappeared.


01:51:57.860 --> 01:52:01.030
That understood any
kind of service in that economy


01:52:01.062 --> 01:52:03.800
sought a profit,
and in the case of a loan,


01:52:03.833 --> 01:52:06.869
that came in the form
of a fee called interest.


01:52:06.901 --> 01:52:10.205
So the borrower not only had
to eventually repay the loan


01:52:10.239 --> 01:52:13.009
but also the interest
charged as well.


01:52:14.043 --> 01:52:16.312
Imagine an
island of a hundred people,


01:52:16.345 --> 01:52:19.882
they decide to organize
themselves through market economy.


01:52:19.914 --> 01:52:22.385
They plop a bank down
and each of them take a loan


01:52:22.418 --> 01:52:25.922
for 100 credits of money
at ten percent interest.


01:52:25.954 --> 01:52:28.557
So they all now have
10,000 credits total


01:52:28.591 --> 01:52:31.227
in their money supply
and they begin to work


01:52:31.260 --> 01:52:34.196
in exchange creating
economic activity.


01:52:34.230 --> 01:52:36.432
When the time comes
to pay back the loan,


01:52:36.464 --> 01:52:40.101
they realized they owe
not only the 100 credits,


01:52:40.135 --> 01:52:43.972
but the ten percent interest,
so 110 credits.


01:52:44.006 --> 01:52:46.042
Same for the whole society,


01:52:46.074 --> 01:52:49.077
in total everyone on
the island now owes the bank


01:52:49.110 --> 01:52:51.079
11,000 credits.


01:52:51.113 --> 01:52:55.318
But yet, only 10,000 actually
exist in the money supply.


01:52:55.351 --> 01:53:00.156
There is now more depth
owed than money in existence


01:53:00.189 --> 01:53:02.024
due to the interest charged.


01:53:02.056 --> 01:53:04.961
So three things can happen:
one, those short


01:53:04.994 --> 01:53:07.230
can take on more loans
to temporarily cover


01:53:07.262 --> 01:53:09.397
the old ones postponing
the problem.


01:53:09.431 --> 01:53:12.268
Two, people could ramp up
competitive trade


01:53:12.301 --> 01:53:14.337
increasing economic activity


01:53:14.369 --> 01:53:17.038
to try to get enough
from others to cover the debt,


01:53:17.071 --> 01:53:20.877
displacing the debt responsibility
like a game of musical chairs.


01:53:20.909 --> 01:53:24.279
Or three, the bank comes in
and takes real property


01:53:24.312 --> 01:53:26.414
to compensate
for the outstanding debt,


01:53:26.448 --> 01:53:30.218
which is inevitably what happens
somewhere down the line anyway.


01:53:30.252 --> 01:53:31.954
Wait, that,
that can't be right.


01:53:31.986 --> 01:53:34.356
That would just be a system
of organized theft.


01:53:34.390 --> 01:53:38.895
Yes, banks were vehicles
of creation on one side,


01:53:38.927 --> 01:53:40.229
and a system of organized theft


01:53:40.262 --> 01:53:42.131
and class oppression
on the other.


01:53:42.163 --> 01:53:45.200
But in a large complex
global society, one based


01:53:45.234 --> 01:53:48.169
on economic growth,
money moves so rapidly


01:53:48.203 --> 01:53:51.007
it was very hard for the mechanics
of this to be recognized.


01:53:51.039 --> 01:53:53.642
Obscured by things
like the boom-and-bust cycle,


01:53:53.676 --> 01:53:56.145
monetary expansion
and contraction.


01:53:57.046 --> 01:54:00.048
- Mm, please continue.
- So back to our island again.


01:54:01.350 --> 01:54:03.686
But this time
for the sake of simplicity,


01:54:03.718 --> 01:54:06.521
let's remove the interest
fee from the equation,


01:54:06.555 --> 01:54:10.559
and focus only on the outcomes
of competitive trade itself.


01:54:10.592 --> 01:54:13.663
<i>So the 10,000 credits
of money has been moving around</i>


01:54:13.695 --> 01:54:15.997
<i>through trade, labor investment,</i>


01:54:16.030 --> 01:54:18.434
<i>starting businesses,
hiring employees,</i>


01:54:18.467 --> 01:54:21.003
<i>and as is inevitable
to the game,</i>


01:54:21.035 --> 01:54:24.506
<i>some businesses will outperform
winning disproportion income,</i>


01:54:24.539 --> 01:54:27.510
<i>while others will fall
behind losing income.</i>


01:54:27.543 --> 01:54:29.979
<i>And naturally
those with more money</i>


01:54:30.012 --> 01:54:32.982
<i>can then increase
their gaming advantage becoming</i>


01:54:33.015 --> 01:54:37.419
<i>ever more competitive and of
course more prone to keep winning.</i>


01:54:37.453 --> 01:54:40.056
As the old adage went,
the rich get richer


01:54:40.088 --> 01:54:41.723
and the poor get poorer.


01:54:41.757 --> 01:54:44.393
A small business with limited
means simply can't compete


01:54:44.426 --> 01:54:47.730
with a larger one that can
outperform them in the same service


01:54:47.762 --> 01:54:50.699
due to having more
resources to work with.


01:54:50.732 --> 01:54:53.468
So on our Island,
we see an inevitable


01:54:53.502 --> 01:54:56.571
point in time where say ten
percent of that population


01:54:56.605 --> 01:54:59.542
managed to acquire
90% of the island's wealth


01:54:59.574 --> 01:55:01.443
while the other
90% of the population


01:55:01.476 --> 01:55:03.578
now has only ten percent.


01:55:03.611 --> 01:55:06.716
By the way, this isn't
some arbitrary assumption,


01:55:06.748 --> 01:55:08.984
this can be modeled
mathematically.


01:55:09.017 --> 01:55:12.087
The dynamics of mass
competitive trade in any society


01:55:12.120 --> 01:55:15.024
always moves toward
disequilibrium.


01:55:15.056 --> 01:55:17.726
So back to my point,
when you put this together


01:55:17.760 --> 01:55:21.564
a displaced debt burden
and the application of interest,


01:55:21.596 --> 01:55:24.432
you can begin to see
the insidiousness.


01:55:24.466 --> 01:55:27.570
An economic process based upon
competitive advantage and trade


01:55:27.602 --> 01:55:31.239
that inevitably consolidates
wealth increasing that advantage.


01:55:31.272 --> 01:55:33.542
Coupled with a financial
system that is charging


01:55:33.574 --> 01:55:36.778
interest on loans that can
never be fully repaid.


01:55:36.811 --> 01:55:39.748
So it's no surprise
that in the early 21st century


01:55:39.781 --> 01:55:43.119
the global economy had
about 200 trillion in debt


01:55:43.151 --> 01:55:45.654
and only 80 trillion
in outstanding currency.


01:55:45.686 --> 01:55:47.589
While in the United States,
then considered


01:55:47.623 --> 01:55:49.558
the richest nation
on the planet,


01:55:49.591 --> 01:55:53.396
half of the population had less
than 1,000 dollars in savings


01:55:53.428 --> 01:55:56.731
while also spending more each
year than they actually earned.


01:55:56.765 --> 01:55:58.434
Just trying to keep up.


01:55:59.601 --> 01:56:02.071
While on the global level
in nearly 50 percent


01:56:02.104 --> 01:56:04.406
of the population lived
in poverty on less


01:56:04.440 --> 01:56:08.544
than $5.50 a day
as roughly 30 individuals.


01:56:08.577 --> 01:56:14.249
Yes, 30, owned more wealth than
the bottom half, 3.6 billion.


01:56:15.284 --> 01:56:17.787
Now, there are plenty
of other intermitted things


01:56:17.820 --> 01:56:19.555
that contribute
to this disparity.


01:56:20.455 --> 01:56:22.624
Offshore tax havens
for the rich.


01:56:22.658 --> 01:56:26.095
The mythology of trickle-down
economics were government favors


01:56:26.128 --> 01:56:29.532
business over the public's
well-being, gaming strategies


01:56:29.565 --> 01:56:32.835
to restrict the power
of unions and keep wages low,


01:56:32.868 --> 01:56:35.104
various shenanigans
related to this thing


01:56:35.137 --> 01:56:37.339
called the stock market,


01:56:37.372 --> 01:56:41.077
but the financial system
and its use of depth is really


01:56:41.110 --> 01:56:42.578
the foundation of it all.


01:56:42.610 --> 01:56:44.312
Wow, you, you,


01:56:44.346 --> 01:56:46.315
you would expect riots
in the streets if people


01:56:46.347 --> 01:56:49.185
- really understood that.
- Well, there eventually were.


01:56:49.217 --> 01:56:51.586
But again, at the time,
people just couldn't see it.


01:56:51.619 --> 01:56:55.256
But, no, it wasn't until
the complete abolition of debt


01:56:55.289 --> 01:56:58.694
on all levels that human slavery
finally ended on this planet.


01:56:59.861 --> 01:57:02.565
Speaking of
awareness I'd like to talk


01:57:02.597 --> 01:57:05.234
a little about
how the awakening started.


01:57:05.266 --> 01:57:07.202
I know Concordia
was instrumental


01:57:07.235 --> 01:57:10.238
to technical change later on,
but what about before that


01:57:10.271 --> 01:57:12.841
perhaps starting
in 20th century?


01:57:12.874 --> 01:57:14.877
Well, it's sporadic.


01:57:14.909 --> 01:57:16.678
The largest move
against this system was


01:57:16.712 --> 01:57:19.615
the Bolshevik Revolution
in Russia inspired by a man


01:57:19.647 --> 01:57:22.618
named Karl Marx, that brought
about the Soviet Union


01:57:22.650 --> 01:57:24.787
which existed
for a couple decades.


01:57:24.820 --> 01:57:27.289
And it employed a top-down
regulation system


01:57:27.321 --> 01:57:29.458
they called communism
but it proved to be


01:57:29.490 --> 01:57:31.392
inefficient and oppressive.


01:57:31.426 --> 01:57:34.396
It was also wildly opposed
by Western capitalist powers,


01:57:34.428 --> 01:57:38.300
which sought to destroy it
by any means necessary.


01:57:38.333 --> 01:57:41.837
Criticism was generally infused
with civil rights movements.


01:57:41.869 --> 01:57:44.873
For example, Mahatma Gandhi,
who helped liberate India


01:57:44.906 --> 01:57:48.244
from Colonial rule,
was notably against the system


01:57:48.276 --> 01:57:50.678
recognizing
its creation of poverty.


01:57:50.712 --> 01:57:54.917
Once saying that "poverty was
the worst form of violence."


01:57:54.949 --> 01:57:56.618
Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.,


01:57:56.651 --> 01:57:59.187
was also steadfast
against capitalism,


01:57:59.221 --> 01:58:01.824
seeing it as a part
of a system of oppression


01:58:01.856 --> 01:58:05.461
fueling racism.
Same for the Black Panther Party


01:58:05.494 --> 01:58:08.564
that had chapters all over
the world in the 1960s.


01:58:08.596 --> 01:58:11.432
You also had more academic
minded organizations


01:58:11.466 --> 01:58:13.334
like the technocracy movement


01:58:13.368 --> 01:58:16.504
largely inspired by famous
economist, Thorstein Veblen,


01:58:16.538 --> 01:58:18.274
who recognize that a society


01:58:18.306 --> 01:58:21.176
run by business people
was a very bad idea.


01:58:21.944 --> 01:58:26.315
<i>And by the 21st century
when economic inequality was reaching</i>


01:58:26.347 --> 01:58:30.519
<i>unprecedented extremes coupled
with a growing ecological crisis</i>


01:58:30.552 --> 01:58:33.322
<i>many more were realizing
something had to be done.</i>


01:58:34.789 --> 01:58:38.493
But there is one that sticks
out to me in the context


01:58:38.526 --> 01:58:41.430
of the value system disorder
present at the time.


01:58:41.462 --> 01:58:44.232
An iconic speech given
by a man named Omar Padillo.


01:58:44.999 --> 01:58:48.236
Omar was born in poverty
in Los Angeles, California.


01:58:48.270 --> 01:58:50.239
And as a young man,
he just happened to win


01:58:50.271 --> 01:58:54.376
the largest state lottery
ever in 2037 and he decided


01:58:54.409 --> 01:58:58.480
to use that money to solve the vast
homeless crisis in his hometown.


01:58:58.512 --> 01:59:02.251
He funded non-profits,
established housing treatment centers.


01:59:02.284 --> 01:59:03.886
Not only getting people
off the streets,


01:59:03.918 --> 01:59:06.488
but really helping them
recover and acclimate.


01:59:06.520 --> 01:59:08.656
Something that hadn't
been done before.


01:59:08.690 --> 01:59:11.427
And they gave him
a Nobel Peace Prize for it.


01:59:11.459 --> 01:59:13.895
But what he had
to say during his speech


01:59:13.928 --> 01:59:15.864
wasn't exactly
what they expected.


01:59:39.020 --> 01:59:40.455
Thank you.


01:59:40.489 --> 01:59:41.757
And while I'm happy for those


01:59:41.789 --> 01:59:43.758
we have helped
over the past few years,


01:59:43.792 --> 01:59:47.762
taking about 75,000 homeless
off the Los Angeles streets,


01:59:47.796 --> 01:59:50.432
I must say that the problem


01:59:50.464 --> 01:59:52.900
at hand runs much deeper
than the poverty


01:59:52.934 --> 01:59:56.437
we see around us.
When I created this program,


01:59:56.471 --> 01:59:59.875
focusing on just
this one regional crises,


01:59:59.908 --> 02:00:02.678
my long-term hope was that
it would set a new precedent.


02:00:02.711 --> 02:00:04.713
That those
who disproportionately benefit


02:00:04.745 --> 02:00:08.350
in this world would be inspired,
step up


02:00:08.382 --> 02:00:11.319
and help take responsibility
for the plight


02:00:11.352 --> 02:00:12.887
of the less fortunate.


02:00:12.921 --> 02:00:15.290
After all, what I have done here


02:00:15.324 --> 02:00:17.793
is merely a patch
that can only help a few.


02:00:17.825 --> 02:00:20.428
For the true source of poverty,


02:00:20.462 --> 02:00:23.665
our social system,
continues to go unaddressed.


02:00:24.665 --> 02:00:27.436
We live in a world
of stories and myths.


02:00:27.468 --> 02:00:30.338
And we've been told that
the vast inequities that we see


02:00:30.372 --> 02:00:33.909
is the price we must pay
for innovation and progress.


02:00:33.941 --> 02:00:35.810
Well, innovation to what end


02:00:35.843 --> 02:00:38.946
and how do we define
this notion of progress?


02:00:38.980 --> 02:00:43.319
For if progress is about how much
one can own, the availability of jobs


02:00:43.351 --> 02:00:46.921
the state of a nation's GDP,
the rise of the stock market,


02:00:46.954 --> 02:00:50.425
or the development of some gadget
to entertain and distract you,


02:00:50.458 --> 02:00:53.695
then we face a serious
existential crisis.


02:00:53.729 --> 02:00:57.598
I submit that true progress can
only be measured in the health,


02:00:57.632 --> 02:01:02.338
stability, integrity and responsible
freedom of a civilization.


02:01:02.370 --> 02:01:05.940
Responsible to ourselves,
responsible to each other


02:01:05.973 --> 02:01:09.544
and responsible to their earthly
habitat we all share.


02:01:09.578 --> 02:01:11.847
And by those measures,
my friends,


02:01:11.879 --> 02:01:14.415
there is now little
progress to be found.


02:01:14.449 --> 02:01:16.852
As we all sit idly by,
presupposing


02:01:16.885 --> 02:01:19.789
that the way society works
is the only way it ever could.


02:01:20.721 --> 02:01:23.891
That said, if it's true
that we must persist


02:01:23.925 --> 02:01:26.528
in this inhumane economic order,


02:01:26.561 --> 02:01:29.531
an order that has proven
it can only create affluence


02:01:29.564 --> 02:01:33.436
for a minority at the cost
of destitution for the majority,


02:01:34.735 --> 02:01:37.939
then our only choice
is to seek a new level


02:01:37.972 --> 02:01:40.542
of humanitarian effort.


02:01:40.574 --> 02:01:42.778
Today, three people
have more wealth


02:01:42.811 --> 02:01:46.482
than the bottom 75%
of the world's population,


02:01:46.515 --> 02:01:48.417
six billion people,


02:01:48.449 --> 02:01:51.753
the total wealth of the 4,000
billionaires out there


02:01:51.787 --> 02:01:55.691
have the means to end global
poverty a hundred times over,


02:01:55.723 --> 02:01:59.395
and yet if you study
their philanthropy,


02:01:59.427 --> 02:02:02.131
it is clear that they are
far more concerned


02:02:02.163 --> 02:02:04.867
with their own interests,
their own comforts,


02:02:04.900 --> 02:02:07.870
than working to counter this
ongoing structural violence.


02:02:09.937 --> 02:02:13.141
You see there's a deeper
kind of poverty here.


02:02:14.575 --> 02:02:18.579
A spiritual poverty,
a poverty that grows a culture


02:02:18.613 --> 02:02:22.450
of sociopaths and the more
they have, the more they want,


02:02:22.484 --> 02:02:24.153
and the less they seem
to care otherwise.


02:02:24.186 --> 02:02:28.490
Moral bankruptcy hiding
behind this age-old story


02:02:28.522 --> 02:02:31.793
that one can have a billion dollars
in the bank while others starve


02:02:31.827 --> 02:02:34.864
is somehow natural
to the human condition.


02:02:38.199 --> 02:02:40.668
In a number of months
my program will end


02:02:41.570 --> 02:02:44.106
as the funds will be gone.


02:02:44.138 --> 02:02:48.944
And to date not one wealthy,
so-called philanthropist


02:02:48.976 --> 02:02:51.146
has offered to help keep
the program running.


02:02:54.048 --> 02:02:57.185
Now I know this event
is about peace,


02:02:57.218 --> 02:03:00.655
but it must be understood
that the wealthy of this world,


02:03:00.689 --> 02:03:05.694
those at the root of true
political power are sick.


02:03:05.726 --> 02:03:09.464
Their priorities have nothing
to do with true progress.


02:03:09.498 --> 02:03:12.101
And the time
for tolerance is over.


02:03:13.735 --> 02:03:17.639
The billionaire's of this world
are not symbols of success.


02:03:17.672 --> 02:03:20.676
They are symbols of violence.


02:03:25.113 --> 02:03:27.016
And until that violence ends,


02:03:29.717 --> 02:03:32.253
there will be no peace
on this planet.


02:04:06.754 --> 02:04:08.990
I am sorry, Peter. Can we cut?


02:04:09.958 --> 02:04:11.026
Cut!


02:04:13.194 --> 02:04:15.263
Well, it's, you know,
it's this opening section.


02:04:15.297 --> 02:04:19.635
I'm... I'm still not getting it.
I know we've been through it but, uh,


02:04:19.668 --> 02:04:21.870
- it's just not landing for me.
- I'm just going to keep rolling here.


02:04:21.903 --> 02:04:23.805
Can you grab that
color swatch for me?


02:04:23.837 --> 02:04:25.940
You have to think about
the interpretation in reference


02:04:25.973 --> 02:04:27.976
- to the...
- All right. Thank you.


02:04:30.145 --> 02:04:32.580
This tripod head is toilet.


02:04:35.583 --> 02:04:37.685
You know,
my latte was cold this morning.


02:04:37.718 --> 02:04:39.620
And that's my problem because?


02:04:39.654 --> 02:04:42.723
Okay, okay, I, I think I got it.


02:04:42.757 --> 02:04:44.626
- Thanks.
- No problem. All right


02:04:44.659 --> 02:04:46.161
everybody, let's move.


02:04:46.194 --> 02:04:49.330
Jesus, take a screenwriting
class for Christ's sake.


02:04:49.364 --> 02:04:52.301
No one's going to understand
any of this shit.


02:04:52.333 --> 02:04:53.801
- Camera?
- Rolling.


02:04:53.834 --> 02:04:55.770
- Audio?
- Speeding.


02:04:55.803 --> 02:04:57.071
Slate.


02:04:57.105 --> 02:04:59.341
Scene 37, take 23.


02:05:08.115 --> 02:05:10.886
What if I told you, John,
what many see


02:05:10.918 --> 02:05:15.289
as problems in the world are
actually solutions in transition.


02:05:15.323 --> 02:05:16.825
Is that some kind
of Taoist riddle?


02:05:20.160 --> 02:05:23.332
Poverty, crime, war, disease,
even the ongoing


02:05:23.364 --> 02:05:25.333
destruction of the habitat.


02:05:25.367 --> 02:05:28.102
What if they were
actually productive forces


02:05:28.136 --> 02:05:29.939
assisting a larger end?


02:05:31.038 --> 02:05:33.007
I'd suggest you lighten up
on the Nietzsche.


02:05:37.345 --> 02:05:40.649
What separate us from
the rest of the animal kingdom


02:05:40.681 --> 02:05:44.118
is that we have
no natural predators.


02:05:44.151 --> 02:05:47.989
Nothing out there to snatch us
up for an afternoon snack.


02:05:48.022 --> 02:05:52.727
We're also uniquely aware of
our own mortality and fight it


02:05:52.761 --> 02:05:56.765
with hospitals, medicine,
inoculations.


02:05:56.797 --> 02:05:59.800
Little stopping us
from reproducing


02:05:59.833 --> 02:06:02.336
to the very limit of our host,


02:06:02.369 --> 02:06:04.305
at least not externally.


02:06:04.338 --> 02:06:08.243
Evolution had to do something
a bit different with us.


02:06:09.310 --> 02:06:14.016
So, instead,
<i>we</i> are our own predators.


02:06:15.115 --> 02:06:17.352
Predator and prey in one.


02:06:19.354 --> 02:06:20.388
How convenient.


02:06:23.190 --> 02:06:26.360
Which explains not only
why humans murder each other


02:06:26.394 --> 02:06:30.132
at a rate unparalleled
by any other species,


02:06:30.164 --> 02:06:34.235
but also why we've generated
a social structure


02:06:34.269 --> 02:06:39.908
that by systemic force further
ensures a consistent rate


02:06:39.940 --> 02:06:41.843
of premature mortality.


02:06:43.177 --> 02:06:47.082
- You mean structural violence.
- Embedded into the very design


02:06:47.114 --> 02:06:48.983
of civilization itself.


02:06:50.318 --> 02:06:52.988
So that is what
the Malthusian Mandate does,


02:06:53.020 --> 02:06:54.889
regulate
how to kill off the week.


02:06:55.890 --> 02:06:59.461
No, the Mandate
isn't a policy of action.


02:06:59.494 --> 02:07:02.764
It's a policy of inaction,
a commitment


02:07:02.797 --> 02:07:05.901
not to interfere with the
natural course of the system.


02:07:07.202 --> 02:07:09.870
So the invisible hand
of the market has a machete.


02:07:16.377 --> 02:07:18.245
I don't expect
to win you over, John.


02:07:18.279 --> 02:07:20.214
I'm just telling you
the way it is.


02:07:20.248 --> 02:07:21.817
I agree it's ugly.


02:07:21.850 --> 02:07:23.718
But without the premature death


02:07:23.752 --> 02:07:26.788
that capitalism brings
in the form of inequality


02:07:26.820 --> 02:07:30.091
that planet would have flown
off its access long ago.


02:07:32.894 --> 02:07:33.962
As you know,


02:07:34.962 --> 02:07:37.298
the Industrial Revolution
set in motion


02:07:37.332 --> 02:07:40.736
population growth
that was hyperbolic.


02:07:40.769 --> 02:07:43.805
And out of the 70 million
who now die each year


02:07:43.837 --> 02:07:46.774
30 million do so
because of unequal conditions.


02:07:47.542 --> 02:07:49.211
So 40 percent
of all global deaths


02:07:49.244 --> 02:07:50.779
are structurally inflicted,


02:07:50.811 --> 02:07:52.446
you know,
there's a word for that, Simon.


02:07:52.480 --> 02:07:54.149
Oh, don't be dramatic.


02:07:54.181 --> 02:07:57.251
Again, this is system-level
behavior, John.


02:07:57.284 --> 02:08:00.187
Not some nefarious conspiracy.


02:08:00.221 --> 02:08:02.357
You want to know
what the population would be


02:08:02.390 --> 02:08:03.925
if this wasn't the case?


02:08:03.958 --> 02:08:06.895
If we removed inequality
driven mortality


02:08:06.927 --> 02:08:10.231
for the last 100 years
accounting for fertility,


02:08:10.265 --> 02:08:12.434
about 16 billion
would be sucking up


02:08:12.467 --> 02:08:14.836
resources on that planet today


02:08:14.869 --> 02:08:18.906
with a carrying capacity
still at only ten billion.


02:08:18.940 --> 02:08:21.009
And you think
things are messing now.


02:08:22.342 --> 02:08:24.311
First of all, Simon.


02:08:24.345 --> 02:08:26.981
When the great Reverend
Thomas Malthus decided


02:08:27.015 --> 02:08:29.851
population would forever
outpace resources,


02:08:29.883 --> 02:08:31.520
only one billion existed.


02:08:31.552 --> 02:08:34.890
We're almost ten times that
now despite his projections.


02:08:34.922 --> 02:08:36.223
Second, in the modern era,


02:08:36.257 --> 02:08:37.559
the greatest predictor
of regional


02:08:37.592 --> 02:08:40.028
overpopulation
is poverty itself.


02:08:40.061 --> 02:08:42.898
If the world ever did abolish
it, increasing education,


02:08:42.931 --> 02:08:45.200
population growth
would dramatically slow


02:08:45.232 --> 02:08:47.936
likely approaching equilibrium.


02:08:47.968 --> 02:08:50.404
Your 16 billion number
doesn't account for that.


02:08:50.437 --> 02:08:52.440
And third,
you're completely disregarding


02:08:52.472 --> 02:08:54.475
what the Fullerian study
proved long ago,


02:08:54.508 --> 02:08:56.578
a study sanctioned
by your own department.


02:08:56.610 --> 02:08:59.980
The Fullerian study
was purely theoretical, John.


02:09:00.013 --> 02:09:03.185
A model only possible
if humans magically conform


02:09:03.217 --> 02:09:06.854
to strict sustainability
and efficiency principles.


02:09:06.887 --> 02:09:09.557
It required
a completely egalitarian


02:09:09.591 --> 02:09:12.260
structure
without money and markets.


02:09:12.293 --> 02:09:16.565
A fantasy given once again
the reality of human nature.


02:09:16.597 --> 02:09:19.133
Fantasy or not,
the study was clear.


02:09:19.167 --> 02:09:21.837
Not only can the Earth
hold upwards of 30 billion,


02:09:21.869 --> 02:09:24.271
it can do so with each having
a standard of living equivalent


02:09:24.305 --> 02:09:26.074
to today's upper-middle-class.


02:09:26.106 --> 02:09:29.043
Yeah, again,
assuming equal distribution,


02:09:29.077 --> 02:09:30.544
which is absurd.


02:09:30.578 --> 02:09:32.547
Humans have infinite wants.


02:09:32.579 --> 02:09:35.182
No... they don't.


02:09:35.216 --> 02:09:37.986
Infinite wants
is a value disorder,


02:09:38.019 --> 02:09:41.056
inspired by an economy that needs
infinite consumption to work.


02:09:41.088 --> 02:09:44.158
People are just as prone to be
minimalist as they are materialist.


02:09:44.191 --> 02:09:46.293
Comes down
to the social condition.


02:09:46.327 --> 02:09:49.030
Today, if people didn't have
highly acquisitive values,


02:09:50.030 --> 02:09:51.632
the entire economy
would collapse.


02:09:51.665 --> 02:09:53.968
Fine, believe what you want,
John.


02:09:54.002 --> 02:09:56.037
It's all moot anyway.


02:09:56.070 --> 02:09:58.073
You asked me
what the Malthusian Mandate


02:09:58.105 --> 02:10:00.007
was and I'm telling you.


02:10:00.040 --> 02:10:01.275
Whether you like it or not,


02:10:01.309 --> 02:10:04.245
this is the reality
of things today.


02:10:09.383 --> 02:10:10.985
We got Mandate metadata,


02:10:11.019 --> 02:10:12.287
please tell me
this is recording.


02:10:12.320 --> 02:10:13.288
It certainly is.


02:10:14.555 --> 02:10:16.458
Looks like John
got his subterfuge.


02:10:17.557 --> 02:10:19.426
So how's this organized then?


02:10:19.459 --> 02:10:22.963
- Tracking demographics and mechanisms?
- We are.


02:10:22.997 --> 02:10:25.200
As you'll notice conditions
related to absolute


02:10:25.232 --> 02:10:27.468
poverty in the third world
countries account


02:10:27.502 --> 02:10:30.305
for about 40 percent
of all premature deaths.


02:10:30.337 --> 02:10:32.339
And I see you're also tracking
poverty related illness


02:10:32.373 --> 02:10:34.476
and violence
in the industrialized nations.


02:10:34.508 --> 02:10:37.578
With heart diseases,
cancer and diabetes


02:10:37.611 --> 02:10:39.180
remaining at the top,


02:10:39.212 --> 02:10:41.348
while suicide,
inner-city gang warfare


02:10:41.382 --> 02:10:44.286
and drug overdoses
coming a close second.


02:10:44.319 --> 02:10:46.421
What about deep
stomach relationships?


02:10:46.454 --> 02:10:48.023
Lack of education,
childhood stress?


02:10:48.056 --> 02:10:50.091
Correlated as well.


02:10:50.123 --> 02:10:52.327
Actually, very consistent.


02:10:52.360 --> 02:10:56.330
Regional cycles of deprivation
are like clockwork.


02:10:56.364 --> 02:11:00.101
Poor families continue
to produce more poor families,


02:11:00.133 --> 02:11:03.238
- even in the richest states.
- And the mechanisms?


02:11:03.270 --> 02:11:06.340
Standard class war stuff.
Only difference now


02:11:06.373 --> 02:11:09.010
is ecological
and climate crisis,


02:11:09.043 --> 02:11:11.179
which has rapidly
increased mortality


02:11:11.212 --> 02:11:14.449
in poverty-stricken desert
and coastal regions.


02:11:14.481 --> 02:11:16.484
But the same story otherwise.


02:11:16.516 --> 02:11:19.053
The rich get richer
with disproportional


02:11:19.087 --> 02:11:20.689
opportunity in capital.


02:11:20.721 --> 02:11:22.256
The political establishment


02:11:22.289 --> 02:11:24.525
favors business
and wealthy interests


02:11:24.559 --> 02:11:26.994
over social support programs,


02:11:27.028 --> 02:11:31.065
and the banking system keeps
a solid stranglehold on social


02:11:31.098 --> 02:11:36.203
mobility by saturating the lower
class in insurmountable debt.


02:11:36.236 --> 02:11:38.138
Same on the global level


02:11:38.172 --> 02:11:40.508
through international
finance institutions,


02:11:40.540 --> 02:11:44.511
structural adjustments,
austerity sanctions.


02:11:44.544 --> 02:11:47.382
In fact,
the financial system is really


02:11:47.414 --> 02:11:50.284
the glue that holds
all this together


02:11:50.318 --> 02:11:52.686
keeping constant
downward pressure


02:11:52.720 --> 02:11:55.289
on the impecunious masses.


02:14:02.883 --> 02:14:07.855
<i>Final warning.
Please evacuate proximal region.</i>


02:14:09.156 --> 02:14:12.860
<i>Program will commence in ten,</i>


02:14:12.894 --> 02:14:19.501
<i>nine, eight, seven, six,</i>


02:14:19.534 --> 02:14:22.637
<i>five, four...</i>


02:15:01.242 --> 02:15:04.512
Centuries ago humans
discovered hydrocarbon energy,


02:15:04.544 --> 02:15:06.881
fossil fuels,
and for a good chunk of time,


02:15:06.913 --> 02:15:10.350
it was a critical mechanism
advancing civilization,


02:15:10.383 --> 02:15:12.386
but after a while
it became obvious that


02:15:12.419 --> 02:15:15.923
its continued use posed
insurmountable repercussions,


02:15:15.957 --> 02:15:17.892
damaging the environment.


02:15:17.925 --> 02:15:20.328
So we eventually had
to stop using it completely,


02:15:20.360 --> 02:15:23.430
figuring out other means.
And this is a good analogy


02:15:23.463 --> 02:15:27.668
as to why we also needed
to transcend that social system.


02:15:27.702 --> 02:15:29.537
I look at capitalism


02:15:29.570 --> 02:15:32.874
as an adolescent stage
in the growth of civilization.


02:15:32.906 --> 02:15:36.543
Let's let loose and have people
be selfish building and creating


02:15:36.577 --> 02:15:40.614
in a belligerent manner
with no regard for consequences.


02:15:40.647 --> 02:15:43.618
And we learned a lot.
I think without this phase,


02:15:43.650 --> 02:15:46.687
we wouldn't have been able
to recognize and amplify


02:15:46.721 --> 02:15:49.624
what really makes us
unique as a species.


02:15:49.656 --> 02:15:52.493
We started as DNA
moving from simplicity


02:15:52.525 --> 02:15:55.796
to complexity evolving
a brain with consciousness,


02:15:55.829 --> 02:15:58.365
while blessed
with a profound social nature,


02:15:58.399 --> 02:16:00.968
merging us into a truly
global consciousness


02:16:01.002 --> 02:16:03.571
continuing this expansion.


02:16:03.604 --> 02:16:06.374
Not through our biology
but through the sharing


02:16:06.406 --> 02:16:09.276
of knowledge,
cultural evolution.


02:16:10.444 --> 02:16:13.615
There was a great library
in a city called Alexandria


02:16:13.647 --> 02:16:16.484
long, long ago, and
it contained some of the most


02:16:16.516 --> 02:16:19.553
foundational texts
of human civilization.


02:16:19.587 --> 02:16:22.323
And sadly
it was destroyed in war.


02:16:22.355 --> 02:16:24.591
Many centuries later,
a famous astronomer named


02:16:24.624 --> 02:16:26.927
Carl Sagan,
commented on the subject,


02:16:38.472 --> 02:16:41.042
So the great question
of scientific and hence,


02:16:41.074 --> 02:16:44.545
economic progress,
inevitably becomes,


02:16:50.518 --> 02:16:53.354
How do we harness
our different talents and skills


02:16:53.386 --> 02:16:55.890
to bring out our best potential,


02:16:55.922 --> 02:16:59.060
not only as individuals,
but as a civilization?


02:16:59.092 --> 02:17:01.329
We know the hardware,
so to speak.


02:17:01.361 --> 02:17:04.298
A finite yet profoundly
regenerative planet


02:17:04.331 --> 02:17:05.999
bound by laws of nature


02:17:06.033 --> 02:17:08.836
with our species part
of a delicate ecosystem


02:17:08.868 --> 02:17:11.038
sharing common ground.


02:17:11.072 --> 02:17:13.675
The true measure
of economic progress


02:17:13.707 --> 02:17:15.943
is simply doing more with less.


02:17:15.975 --> 02:17:19.780
Efficiency, the ability to build
something for a given purpose


02:17:19.813 --> 02:17:23.417
that is not only better than
what came before it in utility,


02:17:23.450 --> 02:17:26.753
but also better in terms
of reducing the amount of labor,


02:17:26.786 --> 02:17:30.057
energy and resources
required to make it work.


02:17:30.090 --> 02:17:33.827
Which means it all
comes down to design.


02:17:34.795 --> 02:17:36.698
And back to my point
about markets,


02:17:36.731 --> 02:17:39.066
the infrastructure
it created set the groundwork


02:17:39.099 --> 02:17:42.869
for powerful new means
to merge human talent and skill.


02:17:42.902 --> 02:17:46.006
We just needed to remove
the counter-productive aspects.


02:17:46.039 --> 02:17:48.842
And, needless to say,
wasteful human competition,


02:17:48.875 --> 02:17:52.946
proprietary knowledge, and people
motivated to sell things over and over


02:17:52.980 --> 02:17:57.018
to feed a system of infinite
growth wasn't going to work.


02:17:57.051 --> 02:18:00.822
There had to be a way to bridge
minds and solve problems directly,


02:18:00.855 --> 02:18:04.559
not by proxy of market
competition and profit.


02:18:04.591 --> 02:18:06.993
I think the smartest thing
we ever did as a society


02:18:07.027 --> 02:18:11.132
was the adoption of an open
source, shared resource commons.


02:18:11.164 --> 02:18:14.702
It exponentially catapulted
our problem solving creativity.


02:18:14.734 --> 02:18:17.571
We ended corporations,
localized communities,


02:18:17.605 --> 02:18:19.573
and shared all knowledge.


02:18:19.607 --> 02:18:21.409
In fact,
if it wasn't for that move,


02:18:21.441 --> 02:18:23.744
I really don't think we would've
solved the climate crisis


02:18:23.777 --> 02:18:26.446
and all the other ecological
and social problems


02:18:26.480 --> 02:18:28.116
we faced
before the Great Transition.


02:18:29.082 --> 02:18:32.720
I still stand in awe today
at the stunningly productive


02:18:32.752 --> 02:18:35.489
collective design
processes we created,


02:18:35.522 --> 02:18:39.726
where status is driven not by
differential competition for gain,


02:18:39.759 --> 02:18:42.129
but by the degree
of your contribution:


02:18:42.162 --> 02:18:45.031
how dedicated you are
to problem solving and creation,


02:18:45.064 --> 02:18:48.970
working to improve
the fabric of society itself.


02:18:49.002 --> 02:18:52.706
We also realized the true
purpose of a means of production


02:18:52.740 --> 02:18:55.176
based upon automated technology.


02:18:55.208 --> 02:18:57.578
Not as some brute
industrial mechanism


02:18:57.610 --> 02:19:00.481
to produce an endless
stream of arbitrary goods,


02:19:00.513 --> 02:19:04.018
but as a way to free ourselves
from uncreative labor,


02:19:04.051 --> 02:19:07.588
not to mention improving
efficiency and safety.


02:19:07.620 --> 02:19:09.857
And one final
evolution worth noting


02:19:09.890 --> 02:19:12.693
was the removal
of the price system.


02:19:12.725 --> 02:19:15.128
People stuck these numbers
on everything


02:19:15.161 --> 02:19:18.899
that suggested
some kind of earthly value.


02:19:18.932 --> 02:19:22.937
The numbers were a result
of a particularly crude equation


02:19:22.970 --> 02:19:25.473
dealing with the supply
and demand.


02:19:25.506 --> 02:19:27.775
And while the high priests
of the market religion


02:19:27.807 --> 02:19:30.845
saw those price decrees
as the word of God,


02:19:30.877 --> 02:19:34.815
the truth was any price value
determined by market dynamics alone


02:19:34.849 --> 02:19:36.918
was woefully incomplete.


02:19:36.950 --> 02:19:38.852
And the only term to know
in regard to that


02:19:38.885 --> 02:19:41.721
is negative market externality.


02:19:41.754 --> 02:19:45.827
These are cost values unaccounted
for by the market price equation


02:19:45.859 --> 02:19:48.028
related to damage
done by industry.


02:19:48.062 --> 02:19:50.465
For example,
in the early 21st century,


02:19:50.498 --> 02:19:54.836
the running price of hydrocarbon
energy was in a particular range.


02:19:54.868 --> 02:19:57.003
But yet,
there was actually an additional


02:19:57.036 --> 02:20:00.675
5.3 trillion dollars
in cost every year


02:20:00.707 --> 02:20:02.843
as people worked
to clean up the damage


02:20:02.876 --> 02:20:06.012
the use of hydrocarbons
was doing to the planet.


02:20:06.045 --> 02:20:09.950
Same for the plastics
industry, a serious problem back then.


02:20:09.983 --> 02:20:15.555
It had an externalized cost
of 2.5 trillion dollars a year


02:20:15.589 --> 02:20:17.792
just to clean up the oceans.


02:20:17.824 --> 02:20:19.759
In fact, if you went back


02:20:19.793 --> 02:20:22.762
and did the accounting
for global industry as a whole


02:20:22.795 --> 02:20:25.499
factoring in these negative
market externalities,


02:20:25.533 --> 02:20:28.569
again, these costs not reflected
in the set prices,


02:20:28.601 --> 02:20:31.571
you would find that
no company on the planet


02:20:31.605 --> 02:20:33.173
was actually even profitable.


02:20:34.073 --> 02:20:37.777
So, of course today we have a very
different system of accounting.


02:20:37.811 --> 02:20:42.182
We know almost exactly what's happening
or could happen in downstream effects


02:20:42.215 --> 02:20:46.686
and we improve our total system efficiency
every single year because of it.


02:20:46.720 --> 02:20:49.189
It's a true economy,
in other words.


02:20:50.257 --> 02:20:53.727
And all of this creates a
very different social atmosphere.


02:20:53.760 --> 02:20:56.296
Today our incentives
are aligned.


02:20:56.330 --> 02:20:58.866
No one cuts corners,
there's no reason to.


02:20:58.899 --> 02:21:01.068
No one is trying
to improve some bottom line


02:21:01.100 --> 02:21:03.637
by disregarding
our ecological stewardship


02:21:03.670 --> 02:21:05.772
or the well-being of others.


02:21:05.805 --> 02:21:07.908
We finally got it right.


02:21:07.941 --> 02:21:09.743
And I compare
the footage of the way


02:21:09.777 --> 02:21:13.080
people behaved back then
to the way they do now.


02:21:13.113 --> 02:21:17.885
It's an astounding amount of pride
and community, meaning and purpose.


02:21:17.918 --> 02:21:20.654
They don't feel alone.


02:21:20.688 --> 02:21:24.058
They know they have support,
not just from their friends and family,


02:21:24.090 --> 02:21:27.294
but from the very design
of the social system itself,


02:21:28.261 --> 02:21:30.731
a system designed
to actually care.


02:21:33.233 --> 02:21:34.135
Imagine that.


02:24:21.367 --> 02:24:23.303
The low polygon people are here.


02:24:30.243 --> 02:24:33.114
I wish they'd go back to their own resolution.


02:26:10.577 --> 02:26:13.413
How are you still standing?
What is that your tenth drink?


02:26:21.654 --> 02:26:22.856
Apple juice.


02:26:25.091 --> 02:26:26.126
What's that?


02:26:27.627 --> 02:26:30.497
That is a breach alarm.


02:26:30.529 --> 02:26:33.400
Looks like Orion
is continuing through our security.


02:26:34.367 --> 02:26:37.437
And on that note, John,
I need to know your intent.


02:26:37.471 --> 02:26:41.307
I've explained the Mandate and how
it's far bigger than both of us.


02:26:41.340 --> 02:26:44.043
Policy of inaction is still
a policy of action, Simon.


02:26:44.077 --> 02:26:46.347
Well, if you'd like,
we could continue


02:26:46.379 --> 02:26:48.414
this colorful debate
another time.


02:26:48.447 --> 02:26:50.851
Assuming you're willing
to assist us here now.


02:26:53.420 --> 02:26:56.190
Signal source,
what are the regional markers?


02:26:58.926 --> 02:27:01.127
Well...


02:27:01.161 --> 02:27:02.596
...that's part of the problem.


02:27:02.628 --> 02:27:04.464
The best we have
is a desert region


02:27:04.498 --> 02:27:05.932
on the west side
of North America


02:27:05.965 --> 02:27:08.068
about 10,000 square miles.


02:27:08.100 --> 02:27:10.403
It's not too horrible.
I assume your satellites


02:27:10.437 --> 02:27:12.206
have been scanning
more remote terrain.


02:27:12.239 --> 02:27:15.242
Of course, nothing out
of the ordinary has been seen.


02:27:15.275 --> 02:27:18.279
What about surveillance gaps?
Are the satellite passes seamless?


02:27:18.312 --> 02:27:21.448
For the most part,
there are some periodic latitudinal gaps,


02:27:21.481 --> 02:27:23.517
but they only last a few hours.


02:27:23.550 --> 02:27:26.587
Is it possible Orion is aware
of them? Exploiting them?


02:27:28.622 --> 02:27:31.224
- That's what I'd do.
- I suppose,


02:27:31.258 --> 02:27:32.693
but highly unlikely.


02:27:32.725 --> 02:27:34.627
They would have
to already be in our system


02:27:34.661 --> 02:27:36.297
to know the trajectories.


02:27:37.263 --> 02:27:38.331
Show me the gaps.


02:27:41.600 --> 02:27:42.636
You want my help or not?


02:27:50.743 --> 02:27:52.212
Zoom into the area in question.


02:27:54.348 --> 02:27:55.582
Perfect.


02:27:55.615 --> 02:27:57.184
Hold it right there, John.


02:27:58.685 --> 02:28:01.221
We've already conducted
sub sonar scans.


02:28:01.253 --> 02:28:04.490
If they're underground, they're
using some kind of reflective shield.


02:28:04.524 --> 02:28:06.293
But what I think
would be best for you


02:28:06.325 --> 02:28:08.428
is to analyze
the signal code itself,


02:28:08.462 --> 02:28:10.364
see if you can find a signature.


02:28:14.434 --> 02:28:15.436
John?


02:28:16.570 --> 02:28:19.172
Yeah, sorry,
I was just thinking.


02:28:20.406 --> 02:28:24.178
Hey, remember that Aqua Terraformation
project we worked on years ago?


02:28:25.679 --> 02:28:27.715
Sounds like you need
to get some sleep.


02:28:27.748 --> 02:28:30.083
Your attention span is going.


02:28:30.116 --> 02:28:32.118
And of course...


02:28:32.152 --> 02:28:36.457
...how can I forget?
Ionized nanotech pop-up islands


02:28:36.490 --> 02:28:37.524
from seawater.


02:28:37.556 --> 02:28:39.759
Too bad it never worked.


02:28:39.793 --> 02:28:41.595
We could've extended populations


02:28:41.627 --> 02:28:44.063
into the ocean,
free up some space.


02:28:44.097 --> 02:28:44.999
Yeah.


02:28:45.965 --> 02:28:48.334
What other ambitious
stuff did we work on?


02:28:48.367 --> 02:28:49.703
Those were some exciting times.


02:28:51.037 --> 02:28:52.305
Remember TRD Hollow Cloak?


02:28:52.339 --> 02:28:54.074
Huh!


02:28:54.107 --> 02:28:55.509
A sci-fi classic.


02:28:55.542 --> 02:28:58.079
Tactile remote drone hologram.


02:28:59.111 --> 02:29:01.482
We played with that
for a while here,


02:29:01.515 --> 02:29:03.017
but proved impossible,


02:29:03.050 --> 02:29:05.351
light just can't
merge like that.


02:29:05.384 --> 02:29:07.320
Yeah. Too bad.


02:29:08.455 --> 02:29:12.026
Lots of uses for a fully controlled
remote tactile human hologram.


02:29:39.218 --> 02:29:40.120
Cool, huh?


02:29:46.526 --> 02:29:48.361
And it's at this juncture,
Simon,


02:29:48.394 --> 02:29:49.729
I'm afraid I have
to deliver some kind


02:29:49.762 --> 02:29:51.597
of protagonistical declaration


02:29:51.631 --> 02:29:53.500
of moral superiority


02:29:53.533 --> 02:29:56.337
to indicate the philosophical
error of your ways.


02:29:57.471 --> 02:29:58.305
So here it goes.


02:30:00.140 --> 02:30:02.742
Those that seek
to create in this world,


02:30:02.776 --> 02:30:06.113
those who embrace change
as a natural force,


02:30:06.145 --> 02:30:09.449
helping to unify
humankind as one entity


02:30:09.483 --> 02:30:11.418
in one shared direction,


02:30:11.450 --> 02:30:13.753
realizing
that injustice anywhere


02:30:13.786 --> 02:30:15.388
is injustice everywhere,


02:30:16.456 --> 02:30:20.160
will always be one step ahead
of the traditionalists,


02:30:20.193 --> 02:30:22.662
the preservers, the elitists,


02:30:22.696 --> 02:30:26.733
who, in defense of their separatist
identities and egoist fears,


02:30:26.766 --> 02:30:32.138
seek to divide, conquer,
oppress and destroy.


02:30:33.206 --> 02:30:36.176
The pursuit of livingry
will always be one step ahead


02:30:36.208 --> 02:30:37.410
of the pursuit of weaponry.


02:30:40.614 --> 02:30:43.617
Orion doesn't exist, does it?


02:30:43.650 --> 02:30:45.385
Nope.


02:30:45.418 --> 02:30:47.221
We just put a virus
in your firewall.


02:30:48.420 --> 02:30:50.756
Why?
What's the point of all of this?


02:30:50.789 --> 02:30:52.526
To expose the Mandate,
of course,


02:30:52.559 --> 02:30:53.593
which will be leaked shortly


02:30:53.626 --> 02:30:54.660
to every major news network.


02:30:55.861 --> 02:30:58.899
Oh, seriously, that's it?


02:30:58.931 --> 02:31:01.901
You think we can't absorb that?


02:31:01.935 --> 02:31:04.537
That we haven't perfected
endless ways


02:31:04.571 --> 02:31:07.708
to deflate and confuse
public perception when needed?


02:31:07.741 --> 02:31:10.511
Well, then I guess
you have nothing to worry about.


02:31:11.477 --> 02:31:12.545
See you around, Simon.


02:31:28.428 --> 02:31:32.199
- Hey, token white guy is back!
- Shut up.


02:31:32.232 --> 02:31:33.934
All right, folks.
We don't have much time.


02:31:33.966 --> 02:31:35.902
I don't think he's going
to buy that story for long.


02:31:35.936 --> 02:31:37.671
How're we doing?


02:31:37.704 --> 02:31:40.306
Satellite coordinates locked,
everything's ready.


02:31:40.340 --> 02:31:42.876
But keep in mind,
even with bypassing your surveillance,


02:31:42.909 --> 02:31:45.511
once this thing hits, the heat
signature is going to be out of control.


02:31:45.545 --> 02:31:47.681
That's what
the subterfuge is for.


02:31:47.714 --> 02:31:50.217
- Mandate leak on the blockchain yet?
- Packaging now.


02:31:50.250 --> 02:31:52.586
Should be in the hands of every major
media outlet in about 20 minutes.


02:31:52.618 --> 02:31:54.488
Good.


02:31:54.520 --> 02:31:56.890
Don't forget to show
Simon's stupid face.


02:31:56.922 --> 02:32:00.427
So this is it folks. We have a clear
path avoiding GSA surveillance.


02:32:00.459 --> 02:32:02.428
Once the Mandate exposure
hits the press,


02:32:02.462 --> 02:32:04.698
Simon and company
will be in damage control,


02:32:04.731 --> 02:32:06.634
hopefully long enough
so we can pull this off.


02:32:07.833 --> 02:32:08.868
Anybody need anything?


02:32:08.902 --> 02:32:10.337
- Music.
- Music.


02:32:10.369 --> 02:32:11.739
- Music.
- Music.


02:32:13.240 --> 02:32:13.940
You got it.


02:33:44.063 --> 02:33:46.332
- - All
right, everybody, come on.


02:33:46.366 --> 02:33:48.802
We got... we got to finish
this goddamn movie already.


02:33:48.834 --> 02:33:51.738
Left. Right. Left.


02:34:24.536 --> 02:34:26.539
Responding
to this new leak by Concordia,


02:34:26.572 --> 02:34:28.708
purporting to reveal
a policy of neglect,


02:34:28.741 --> 02:34:30.409
where the death
of millions in poverty


02:34:30.443 --> 02:34:31.945
was deliberately accentuated


02:34:31.977 --> 02:34:34.348
by International Trade policy.


02:34:34.381 --> 02:34:36.415
Leaked documents even include
what appears to be


02:34:36.448 --> 02:34:38.985
a video of GSA's current head,
Simon Devoe.


02:34:47.393 --> 02:34:48.728
Don't look at me like that.


02:34:48.761 --> 02:34:51.364
Standard operating procedure,
folks.


02:34:51.397 --> 02:34:54.500
Get your media agents out there
and start changing the narrative.


02:35:04.476 --> 02:35:05.979
Sir.


02:35:07.913 --> 02:35:09.649
- What is it?
- I don't know.


02:35:09.681 --> 02:35:12.485
We don't have visual coverage
in that region yet.


02:35:12.518 --> 02:35:13.453
Send the drones.


02:35:29.068 --> 02:35:30.770
Holy shit, it worked.


02:35:30.804 --> 02:35:32.406
Shall we alert the base?


02:35:32.438 --> 02:35:33.139
Indeed.


02:35:34.072 --> 02:35:35.574
The migration begins.


02:35:38.777 --> 02:35:40.880
It's an artificial island, Sir,


02:35:40.913 --> 02:35:44.750
in the Pacific, about 700 miles
off the coast of North America.


02:35:46.786 --> 02:35:49.456
Holy shit, it worked.


02:35:50.723 --> 02:35:52.592
Scramble fighters to destroy it?


02:35:52.625 --> 02:35:55.796
No. See this?


02:35:55.829 --> 02:35:59.466
It's a plasma congealed
electromagnetic field,


02:35:59.499 --> 02:36:01.735
- impenetrable.
- How do you know that?


02:36:02.734 --> 02:36:04.504
Because I know the creator.


02:36:07.539 --> 02:36:09.008
And sing.


02:36:36.768 --> 02:36:39.238
So, we've just arrived
at the colony of Concordia,


02:36:39.271 --> 02:36:41.040
where almost
a million people have migrated


02:36:41.073 --> 02:36:43.876
to basically get away
from the rest of the world.


02:36:43.910 --> 02:36:46.546
We are the first press
allowed in,


02:36:46.579 --> 02:36:48.515
waiting to meet our guide.


02:36:50.682 --> 02:36:53.186
- Hi, I'm Elnoria.
- Nice to meet you.


02:36:53.218 --> 02:36:54.753
Thank you for having us.


02:36:54.786 --> 02:36:56.188
I suggest we move
to the city center,


02:36:56.222 --> 02:36:57.958
start our tour from there.


02:36:57.991 --> 02:37:00.127
You can cut.


02:37:06.099 --> 02:37:08.235
So, there's been a lot
of speculation on the mainland


02:37:08.268 --> 02:37:10.102
about what goes on here.


02:37:10.135 --> 02:37:12.905
You're depicted
as some kind of a cult.


02:37:12.938 --> 02:37:14.740
Claims of human right abuses,


02:37:14.774 --> 02:37:17.843
and your media is being
censored pretty aggressively.


02:37:17.876 --> 02:37:20.045
Well, that's why you're here.


02:37:20.079 --> 02:37:22.616
This island wasn't created
to escape the world,


02:37:22.649 --> 02:37:26.086
it was created to set
an example to change the world,


02:37:26.118 --> 02:37:29.822
show what's actually possible if
humankind decided to work together.


02:37:29.856 --> 02:37:32.057
So,
where would you like to start?


02:37:32.090 --> 02:37:33.959
I guess technicals.


02:37:33.992 --> 02:37:35.528
How are you powering this place?


02:37:36.596 --> 02:37:38.865
Mixed renewable integration.


02:37:38.897 --> 02:37:42.802
The island's core baseload
systems are solar, wind and ocean,


02:37:42.834 --> 02:37:44.937
while localized
kinetic energy capture,


02:37:44.971 --> 02:37:46.706
mixed use, reuse mechanisms,


02:37:46.739 --> 02:37:48.775
are designed
into most everything.


02:37:48.807 --> 02:37:50.109
Like footsteps?


02:37:50.143 --> 02:37:52.045
Footsteps, vehicle motion,


02:37:52.078 --> 02:37:55.982
pipe flows, anything that moves,
we recapture.


02:37:56.015 --> 02:37:58.217
We're at about 5,000
percent efficiency,


02:37:58.250 --> 02:38:00.719
more energy than we know
what to do with.


02:38:00.752 --> 02:38:02.221
That's insane.


02:38:02.254 --> 02:38:03.789
Not really.


02:38:03.822 --> 02:38:04.990
The earth is, in effect,


02:38:05.024 --> 02:38:06.893
a perpetual motion machine.


02:38:06.926 --> 02:38:09.796
You people on the mainland
could easily do the same thing,


02:38:09.829 --> 02:38:13.833
but your economic system simply isn't
conducive to integrative design.


02:38:13.866 --> 02:38:17.070
Speaking of which, let's head to the
development center around the corner.


02:38:17.102 --> 02:38:18.037
Okay.


02:38:24.043 --> 02:38:26.113
This is one
of our design facilities.


02:38:27.245 --> 02:38:29.949
Okay. Like an office.


02:38:31.216 --> 02:38:32.752
So these people are employed.


02:38:34.386 --> 02:38:37.891
Employed. Um, I suppose in the
most technical sense of the word, sure.


02:38:37.923 --> 02:38:39.992
But we have
no systemic slavery here.


02:38:40.026 --> 02:38:43.096
No one is coerced to submit
for their basic survival,


02:38:43.128 --> 02:38:45.632
something I suspect might be
very foreign to you.


02:38:46.866 --> 02:38:49.269
But everyone needs
to do something, right?


02:38:49.302 --> 02:38:53.106
So how do you network skills,
organized trade, markets?


02:38:53.138 --> 02:38:54.807
There is no trade.


02:38:54.840 --> 02:38:57.810
There are no markets.
There is no currency.


02:38:57.843 --> 02:39:00.714
Those who wish to contribute do
so through collaborative design


02:39:00.747 --> 02:39:02.915
in an open source environment.


02:39:02.948 --> 02:39:05.618
What you think of as industries
of production on the mainland


02:39:05.652 --> 02:39:06.920
is unified here.


02:39:06.953 --> 02:39:08.120
Wait, I don't understand.


02:39:09.322 --> 02:39:11.124
These people are
not paid to be here?


02:39:12.925 --> 02:39:14.327
How are they motivated?


02:39:14.359 --> 02:39:16.629
Well, how is anyone motivated?


02:39:16.662 --> 02:39:19.298
Do you need to get paid to get
out of bed in the morning?


02:39:19.331 --> 02:39:21.667
Do you need to be paid
to ensure your own health,


02:39:21.700 --> 02:39:24.003
the health of your family
and friends?


02:39:24.036 --> 02:39:27.906
Paid to show stewardship for the
habitat and society that supports you?


02:39:27.939 --> 02:39:31.243
- How about innovation?
- Innovation to what end?


02:39:31.277 --> 02:39:35.048
To create something to improve
life and experience?


02:39:35.081 --> 02:39:36.750
Or to create something to sell?


02:39:38.318 --> 02:39:42.088
If you think about it, it has been the
blind economic drive toward innovation,


02:39:42.120 --> 02:39:44.423
as you know it, that continues
to lead your society


02:39:44.456 --> 02:39:46.925
- to destruction
- Okay, then.


02:39:46.958 --> 02:39:49.161
Once these people have
designed something, then what?


02:39:50.128 --> 02:39:51.897
If a design
meets proper criteria


02:39:51.930 --> 02:39:54.767
in terms of efficiency
and sustainability protocols,


02:39:54.801 --> 02:39:58.838
it is then accessible by our mostly
additive manufacturing system.


02:39:58.870 --> 02:40:01.173
Additive? 3D printers?


02:40:01.206 --> 02:40:03.976
Which have been perfected
to a degree where modular arrays


02:40:04.009 --> 02:40:07.680
can produce most anything conceived
of with traditional material.


02:40:11.116 --> 02:40:13.285
And by the way,
there's no waste here.


02:40:13.319 --> 02:40:16.021
Our AI designed filters won't
allow production of any item


02:40:16.054 --> 02:40:18.157
that isn't 100% regenerative.


02:40:20.159 --> 02:40:21.961
Sorry, I'm speechless.


02:40:21.993 --> 02:40:23.230
If what you say is true,


02:40:24.162 --> 02:40:25.731
you've actually done it.


02:40:25.765 --> 02:40:26.800
Done what?


02:40:26.832 --> 02:40:28.233
You've created Utopia.


02:40:29.868 --> 02:40:31.904
If you want to sound
like an idiot, sure.


02:40:32.904 --> 02:40:37.009
This isn't Utopia, friend.
It's simply pragmatic design.


02:40:37.043 --> 02:40:39.813
Come, let me now show you
our democratic system,


02:40:39.846 --> 02:40:42.015
